{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_gpS2MS5U7zbpcmRD31UEvsGT","content":"1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-02 11:20:00 GMT\n2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-02 18:20:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n3\tCoding-Agent: vibe (mistral-4.0); codex CLOSED until further notice per the owner\n4\tSession-ID: not-applicable (orchestrator-dispatched, fresh session)\n5\t# Task: H3-0 — restore the declared dispositions and make the kernel-gate evidence trustworthy\n6\t\n7\tRole: QA/harness engineer (mistral-4.0 via vibe). NOTE: your implementation will be code-quality reviewed by a kimi round before landing — write for review.\n8\tReviewer/landing: the ZCode glm orchestrator seat; a compiler-engineer reviewer checks the callable-representation part; the architect reviews the disposition guards.\n9\t\n10\t## Governing instructions\n11\t\n12\tThe architect's hardening-3 plan APPROVED this slice (plan: `collab/1793770000000-architect-hardening-3-design.gpt-6-astra.prompt.md` + its stdout log — read both). Read `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md`, the refreshed `slice9_evidence.edn` / `slice9_unexercised.edn`, and the harness `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` (the classifier is ~line 1932; the gate test ~2235-2300). Work in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-h30`, branch `hardening3-h3-0`, base `6188b98a6` (master). Push the branch; do NOT merge.\n13\t\n14\t## Headless operating constraints (binding)\n15\t\n16\tYou run HEADLESS on the vibe CLI with edit approvals only: file edits are auto-accepted; shell command approvals are NOT available, so any bash call blocks the round forever (measured on another headless agent). Therefore:\n17\t\n18\t- **Do not run shell commands. Not once.** All changes happen through file edits only.\n19\t- The verification commands you WOULD run (the focused gate test, the full oracle namespace, kondo) go into your report as exact command lines; the seat runs them.\n20\t- Do not attempt git operations — the seat owns staging, review, and landing.\n21\t- A previous session created `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn` — read it, keep what is correct, continue from it.\n22\t\n23\t## Scope (harness-only — no compiler changes, no yang.call/yin.vm changes)\n24\t\n25\tWritable: `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`, `test/yang/latte_oracle/*` (evidence/gate records and any new declaration file), `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` (only to refresh stale yang.clojure gate narrative rows). Everything else forbidden.\n26\t\n27\t## The two defects to repair\n28\t\n29\t1. **The evidence writer drops declared dispositions.** `write-kernel-gate-evidence!` regenerates `:recorded-portability-boundaries` as `[]` and no fixture row carries `:status :recorded-deviation`, so the gate test's deviations assertion fails. The declared records are recoverable verbatim from `git show ea18c8e4^:test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn` (see `:recorded-portability-boundaries`): `elab-after-qed` and `check-after-qed`, boundary `:nonportable-host-value`, upstream embeds `clojure.core/meta` in error data, reason verbatim in that history.\n30\t\n31\t2. **The deviation classifier is representation-stale.** The architect's finding: the classifier still requires a bare closure at `:meta` (~line 1932), but the refreshed outcomes contain a §8.10 callable descriptor (the adoption's published representation). Restoring the declarations therefore requires a representation-aware classifier: validate the guest callable using its actual runtime representation — a map containing `{:type :closure}` is insufficient. Do NOT make C-lane callable representations equal merely to obtain agreement; preserve every original outcome and agreement flag.\n32\t\n33\t## Required behavior (the architect's H3-0 acceptance, binding)\n34\t\n35\t- Declarations become explicit, versioned input to classification (a declaration file or clearly-versioned structure in the harness), NOT something generated evidence is the sole source of. Provenance: `ea18c8e4^`.\n36\t- Carrying a declaration forward means REVALIDATING the current fixture against its declared boundary: pinned fixture ID and call, completed A/B/C executions, the original exception message, the script value and collection shape, and the precise host-function/guest-callable boundary. For the two after-qed rows specifically.\n37\t- `typing-ascription` and `compile-malformed` retain their exact guarded upstream-failure dispositions; all four declared exception departures retain scope and provenance.\n38\t- Negative controls (new regressions): a mutated call, an unrelated fixture ID, a changed payload or shape, a forged callable representation, and an incomplete lane must each FAIL classification.\n39\t- Writer round-trip tests: declarations, statuses, raw comparisons, and coverage survive a write+read cycle; ordinary tests stay read-only.\n40\t- Refresh the stale gate narrative (`slice9_gate.md` and the known-gaps rows): neither \"145/165\" nor \"only 20 remain\" describes the baseline — it is 107 credited / 58 unexercised, 100 agreements, 2 deviations, 2 blocked, 2 upstream failures.\n41\t- Expected post-slice gate state, with no other changes: 100 agreements, two deviations, two blocked fixtures, two upstream failures; 107 credited, 58 remaining. The final `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` assertion stays unchanged and still fails (the gate stays :blocked). Any different result requires explanation in the report.\n42\t\n43\t## Verification\n44\t\n45\t- Focused: the gate test (`test-kernel-differential-gate`) — after H3-0 exactly ONE expected failure remains (the blocked assertion), identified by assertion line.\n46\t- The full oracle namespace; the accounting/deviations/blocked assertions each identified; kondo on the touched files; the poisoned-parse/1 and unused-arity regressions preserved.\n47\t- Record real command output for every claim.\n48\t\n49\t## Report\n50\t\n51\tFindings to `collab/` in the worktree (it may reject a flat file — if so, note the path in the branch commit message and leave the file untracked; the seat archives it). Commit on the branch with `test(latte):` prefix; push; do not merge."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_Ssf9B1t2AEVn7M4bE2prbpNM","content":"1\t(ns yang.latte-oracle-test\n2\t  \"Pinned upstream LaTTe differential harness, slices 1-9 of the Yang gap\n3\t   program. A executes the original library on Clojure. B executes explicit\n4\t   portability source on Clojure; C compiles it through Yang for the walker\n5\t   and semantic VMs. Slice 9 fails closed on the full kernel corpus. The\n6\t   legacy classifier records historical blockers;\n7\t   the context module additionally checks free-symbol admission before C.\n8\t   Adaptations, operation sequences and scope departures live beside the\n9\t   manifest in yang/latte_oracle/.\"\n10\t  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n11\t            [clojure.edn :as edn]\n12\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n13\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n14\t            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n15\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n16\t            [clojure.tools.reader :as r]\n17\t            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]\n18\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n19\t            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n20\t            [yang.core.call :as call]\n21\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n22\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n23\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n24\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n25\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n26\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n27\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rows-support]\n28\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n29\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n30\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n31\t            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n32\t\n33\t\n34\t(def ^:private manifest\n35\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\"))))\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t(defn- ns-declaration-aliases\n39\t  \"Alias -> full ns symbol, taken from the file's own (ns ...) declaration —\n40\t   never invented: ::alias/kw must read as :that.real.ns/kw.\"\n41\t  [ns-form]\n42\t  (let [alias-map (atom {})\n43\t        consume-spec (fn [spec]\n44\t                       (when (sequential? spec)\n45\t                         (let [lib (first spec)]\n46\t                           (loop [xs (rest spec)]\n47\t                             (when (seq xs)\n48\t                               (if (= :as (first xs))\n49\t                                 (do (swap! alias-map assoc (second xs) lib)\n50\t                                     (recur (drop 2 xs)))\n51\t                                 (recur (next xs))))))))]\n52\t    (loop [clauses (rest (rest ns-form))]\n53\t      (when (seq clauses)\n54\t        (let [clause (first clauses)]\n55\t          (if (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n56\t            (do (loop [reqs (next clause)]\n57\t                  (let [spec (first reqs)]\n58\t                    (when (and (not (nil? spec)) (not (keyword? spec)))\n59\t                      (consume-spec spec)\n60\t                      (recur (next reqs)))))\n61\t                (recur (next clauses)))\n62\t            (recur (next clauses))))))\n63\t    @alias-map))\n64\t\n65\t\n66\t(defn- read-forms\n67\t  \"Read one latte-kernel source file with reader conditionals resolved for\n68\t   :clj, ::alias/kw keywords resolved against the file's own ns declaration,\n69\t   and ::kw resolved against the file's own namespace — so the C leg compiles\n70\t   the same keyword identities the upstream A leg runs.\"\n71\t  [ns-sym]\n72\t  (let [f (io/resource (str (str/replace (name ns-sym) \".\" \"/\") \".cljc\"))\n73\t        pr (rt/source-logging-push-back-reader (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f)) 1 (str f))\n74\t        ns-form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)\n75\t        declared-name (second ns-form)\n76\t        aliases (ns-declaration-aliases ns-form)]\n77\t    (binding [r/*alias-map* aliases\n78\t              *ns* (the-ns (create-ns declared-name))]\n79\t      (loop [acc []]\n80\t        (let [form (r/read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:clj} :eof ::eof} pr)]\n81\t          (if (= form ::eof) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t(def ^:private all-forms\n85\t  (into {} (map (fn [ns-sym] [ns-sym (read-forms ns-sym)])\n86\t                (distinct (map :ns manifest)))))\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t(def ^:private top-forms\n90\t  (into {} (map (fn [{:keys [ns kind name]}]\n91\t                  [[ns name] (first (filter #(and (seq? %)\n92\t                                                  (= kind (first %))\n93\t                                                  (= name (second %)))\n94\t                                            (get all-forms ns)))]))\n95\t        manifest))\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t(def ^:private scanned-symbols\n99\t  #{'loop 'recur 'case 'throw 'ex-info 'atom 'swap! 'reset! 'lazy-seq 'gensym\n100\t    'apply 'comp 'partial 'reduced 'reduce 'map 'mapv 'filter 'remove 'into\n101\t    'concat 'merge 'str 'symbol 'keyword 'vector 'seq 'nth 'nthnext 'assoc-in\n102\t    'count 'name 'when-let 'if-let 'when-some 'if-some 'cond})\n103\t\n104\t\n105\t(defn- walk-symbols\n106\t  [form]\n107\t  (cond\n108\t    (seq? form) (if (and (= 'quote (first form)) (= 2 (count form)))\n109\t                  #{}\n110\t                  (mapcat walk-symbols form))\n111\t    (vector? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\n112\t    (map? form) (mapcat walk-symbols (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n113\t    (set? form) (mapcat walk-symbols form)\n114\t    (symbol? form) (if (namespace form) #{} #{form})\n115\t    :else #{}))\n116\t\n117\t\n118\t(defn- destructuring?\n119\t  [binding]\n120\t  (not (symbol? binding)))\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t(defn- classify-form\n124\t  [form]\n125\t  (let [[kind _name & body-ops] form\n126\t        fs (atom (into #{} (walk-symbols form)))]\n127\t    (when (and (= 'defn kind) (seq body-ops))\n128\t      (let [second-op (first body-ops)]\n129\t        (cond\n130\t          (seq? second-op) (swap! fs conj :multi-arity)\n131\t          (not (vector? second-op)) (swap! fs conj :docstring)\n132\t          :else (when (some destructuring? second-op)\n133\t                  (swap! fs conj :destructuring)))))\n134\t    (when (and (= 'defn kind) (vector? (first body-ops)))\n135\t      ;; loop/recur inside the params+body\n136\t      (when (some #(contains? % 'recur) (map #(into #{} (walk-symbols %)) (clojure.core/rest body-ops)))\n137\t        (swap! fs conj :recur)))\n138\t    (when (contains? @fs 'loop) (swap! fs conj :loop))\n139\t    (set (filter #(or (contains? scanned-symbols %) (keyword? %)) @fs))))\n140\t\n141\t\n142\t(defn- host-module\n143\t  \"Register `fns` as host module `module-name`, every export `:pure`.\"\n144\t  [registry module-name fns arities]\n145\t  (module/register-host-module\n146\t    registry module-name fns\n147\t    (into {} (map (fn [[op]] [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\n148\t          fns)))\n149\t\n150\t\n151\t(def ^:private kind-fns\n152\t  \"The irreducible kind and name primitives (yang.clojure/kind-module), plus\n153\t   the two host Var primitives the throw-site fixtures reach.\"\n154\t  (assoc yang/kind-module 'var? var? 'resolve resolve))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- oracle-registry\n158\t  \"The stream/data modules, kind primitives, and portable outcome adapters.\n159\t   Slices 1-7 retain their host Var probes; context modules supply only the\n160\t   callback-free kind exports and cannot consult host namespaces.\"\n161\t  ([] (oracle-registry kind-fns))\n162\t  ([kinds]\n163\t   (let [portable (into {}\n164\t                        (map (fn [[source _]]\n165\t                               (let [op (symbol (name source))]\n166\t                                 [op (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\n167\t                                                           (get data/data-module op))])))\n168\t                        yang/library-adapters)]\n169\t     (-> (module/default-registry)\n170\t         module/register-stream-module\n171\t         module/register-cell-module\n172\t         data/register-data-module\n173\t         (host-module 'kind kinds yang/kind-arities)\n174\t         (host-module 'portable portable\n175\t                      (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\n176\t                            (keys portable)))))))\n177\t\n178\t\n179\t(def ^:private arg-vector-opts\n180\t  \"The argument-vector convention with the outcome model, the guest library's\n181\t   adapters and the VM primitives' published profiles as the native names.\"\n182\t  {:convention :arg-vector, :outcomes true\n183\t   :adapters yang/library-adapters\n184\t   :native vm/primitive-profiles})\n185\t\n186\t\n187\t(defn- result-shape\n188\t  \"Collection families and domain metadata, excluding reader provenance.\"\n189\t  [x]\n190\t  [(not-empty (apply dissoc (meta x) [:source :file :line :column :end-line :end-column]))\n191\t   (cond\n192\t     (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k [(result-shape k) (result-shape v)]])) x)\n193\t     (set? x) (into #{} (map (fn [v] [v (result-shape v)])) x)\n194\t     (sequential? x) [(if (vector? x) :vector :sequence) (mapv result-shape x)]\n195\t     :else :scalar)])\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t(defn- unbound-ast-symbols\n199\t  \"Admission for the portable context module: every variable is a lexical\n200\t   binder, declared guest function, or explicitly supplied data primitive.\"\n201\t  [ast program]\n202\t  (let [globals (into #{'yin/def}\n203\t                      (concat (keys vm/primitive-profiles)\n204\t                              (map first call/definitions)\n205\t                              (for [form program :when (#{'def 'defn 'defn-} (first form))]\n206\t                                (second form))\n207\t                              (for [[module exports] {'kind yang/kind-module\n208\t                                                      'cell module/cell-module\n209\t                                                      'data data/data-module\n210\t                                                      'stream module/stream-module\n211\t                                                      'portable (into {} (map (fn [[_ v]] [(symbol (name v)) nil]))\n212\t                                                                      yang/library-adapters)}\n213\t                                    export (keys exports)]\n214\t                                (symbol (str module) (name export)))))]\n215\t    (letfn [(scan\n216\t              [node bound]\n217\t              (case (:type node)\n218\t                :variable (if (or (contains? globals (:name node))\n219\t                                  (contains? bound (:name node))) #{} #{(:name node)})\n220\t                :literal #{}\n221\t                :vm/current-continuation #{}\n222\t                :lambda (scan (:body node) (into bound (:params node)))\n223\t                :application (into (scan (:operator node) bound)\n224\t                                   (mapcat #(scan % bound)) (:operands node))\n225\t                :if (into #{} (mapcat #(scan (get node %) bound))\n226\t                          [:test :consequent :alternate])\n227\t                (throw (ex-info \"Unexpected AST in context admission\" {:type (:type node)}))))]\n228\t      (scan ast #{}))))\n229\t\n230\t\n231\t(defn- run-outcome\n232\t  \"Compile `forms` plus `call-form` (with the library definitions they need)\n233\t   and return the RAW outcome of the call: the value channel carries\n234\t   [tag payload]. Every fixture runs on walker and semantic lanes under the\n235\t   same finite instruction budget.\"\n236\t  ([forms call-form] (run-outcome forms call-form (oracle-registry)))\n237\t  ([forms call-form modules] (run-outcome forms call-form modules false))\n238\t  ([forms call-form modules closed?]\n239\t   (let [program (into [] (concat forms [call-form]))\n240\t         program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n241\t         ast (yang/compile-program program true arg-vector-opts)\n242\t         _ (when closed?\n243\t             (let [unbound (unbound-ast-symbols ast program)]\n244\t               (when (seq unbound)\n245\t                 (throw (ex-info \"Unadmitted context dependencies\" {:symbols unbound})))\n246\t               (is (empty? unbound) \"context program is closed over its supplied modules\")))\n247\t         walker (compiler-test/run-guest-ast ast modules :walker 1000000)\n248\t         semantic (compiler-test/run-guest-ast ast modules :semantic 1000000)]\n249\t     (is (= walker semantic) (str \"oracle lanes agree: \" (pr-str call-form)))\n250\t     (is (= (result-shape walker) (result-shape semantic))\n251\t         (str \"oracle lane shapes and metadata agree: \" (pr-str call-form)))\n252\t     walker)))\n253\t\n254\t\n255\t(defn- run-on-vm\n256\t  \"run-outcome, unwrapped: the call's value, or its error outcome thrown as\n257\t   ex-info carrying the error data.\"\n258\t  [forms call-form]\n259\t  (let [[tag payload] (run-outcome forms call-form)]\n260\t    (if (= :yin.k/ok tag)\n261\t      payload\n262\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"guest error: \" (pr-str payload)) payload)))))\n263\t\n264\t\n265\t(def ^:private clean-forms\n266\t  (for [{:keys [ns name]} manifest\n267\t        :let [f (get top-forms [ns name])]\n268\t        :when (and f (empty? (classify-form f)))]\n269\t    f))\n270\t\n271\t\n272\t(def ^:private fixtures\n273\t  \"qualified-fn | args for the A/C differential. The four anchors the\n274\t   architect named first, plus leaf functions classified :clean.\"\n275\t  {'latte-kernel.defenv/mkenv [[]]\n276\t   'latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [[1 2 3 4] 2]})\n277\t\n278\t\n279\t(defn- upstream-fn\n280\t  [qsym]\n281\t  (requiring-resolve qsym))\n282\t\n283\t\n284\t(deftest test-oracle-classification\n285\t  (testing \"every manifest entry has source\"\n286\t    (is (every? (fn [{:keys [ns name]}] (get top-forms [ns name])) manifest)))\n287\t  (testing \"every binding has an explicit admission decision and reason\"\n288\t    (is (every? #(#{:admitted :excluded} (:disposition %)) manifest))\n289\t    (is (every? #(and (string? (:admission-reason %)) (seq (:admission-reason %))) manifest)))\n290\t  (testing \"architect anchor classifications (slice 1 narrowing table)\"\n291\t    ;; utils/vconcat uses loop/recur\n292\t    (is (contains? (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.utils 'vconcat]))\n293\t                   :loop))\n294\t    ;; utils/pair? is structurally simple but calls host fn `vector` and\n295\t    ;; carries a docstring: both must be classified as blockers\n296\t    (is (contains? (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.utils 'pair?]))\n297\t                   'vector))\n298\t    ;; syntax/alpha-norm is blocked by more than its docstring\n299\t    (is (seq (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.syntax 'alpha-norm]))))\n300\t    ;; nbe/norm is blocked\n301\t    (is (seq (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.nbe 'norm])))))\n302\t  (testing \"A/C differential on admitted fixtures\"\n303\t    (let [results\n304\t          (for [[qsym args] fixtures\n305\t                :let [f (upstream-fn qsym)\n306\t                      a-value (apply f args)\n307\t                      fname (symbol (name qsym))\n308\t                      c-result (try\n309\t                                 {:status :ok\n310\t                                  :value (run-on-vm\n311\t                                           (cond-> (vec clean-forms)\n312\t                                             (not (some #{fname} (map second clean-forms)))\n313\t                                             (conj (get top-forms\n314\t                                                        [(symbol (str/replace (namespace qsym) \"-\" \"_\"))\n315\t                                                         fname])))\n316\t                                           (list* fname args))}\n317\t                                 (catch Exception e\n318\t                                   {:status :error :msg (.getMessage e)}))]]\n319\t            {:qsym qsym, :a a-value, :c c-result})]\n320\t      (doseq [r results]\n321\t        (println \"ORACLE\" (:qsym r) \"A=\" (pr-str (:a r)) \"C=\" (pr-str (:c r))))\n322\t      ;; mkenv: the anchor that must pass end to end today\n323\t      (let [mkenv (first (filter #(= 'latte-kernel.defenv/mkenv (:qsym %)) results))]\n324\t        (is (= :ok (get-in mkenv [:c :status])))\n325\t        (is (= (:a mkenv) (get-in mkenv [:c :value]))))\n326\t      ;; vectorn? is classified blocked by the host stdlib names it uses\n327\t      ;; (vector/count/rem); the guest library now serves them, so A = C\n328\t      (let [v? (first (filter #(= 'latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? (:qsym %)) results))]\n329\t        (is (seq (classify-form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.utils 'vectorn?]))))\n330\t        (is (= :ok (get-in v? [:c :status])))\n331\t        (is (= (:a v?) (get-in v? [:c :value]))))))\n332\t  (testing \"keyword identities read from each file's own ns declaration\"\n333\t    (let [kws (distinct (filter keyword?\n334\t                                (tree-seq coll? identity\n335\t                                          (vec (mapcat val all-forms)))))]\n336\t      ;; ::ascribe in syntax.cljc must read as :latte-kernel.syntax/ascribe\n337\t      (is (contains? (set kws) :latte-kernel.syntax/ascribe))\n338\t      ;; ::prestx/host-constant must resolve through the real alias\n339\t      (is (contains? (set kws) :latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant))\n340\t      ;; no invented namespaces, no caller-namespace leakage\n341\t      (is (not (some #(= \"latte_kernel\" (namespace %)) kws)))\n342\t      (is (not (some #(= \"user\" (namespace %)) kws))))))\n343\t\n344\t\n345\t;; =============================================================================\n346\t;; Slice 3: destructuring anchors now run in the C leg\n347\t;; =============================================================================\n348\t\n349\t(defn- run-with-deps\n350\t  \"Compile the named upstream definitions (dependencies first) plus a call\n351\t   through yang.clojure and run it on the VM; return the call's value.\"\n352\t  [ns-sym dep-names fname args]\n353\t  (let [forms (mapv #(get top-forms [ns-sym %]) dep-names)]\n354\t    (run-on-vm forms (list* fname (map #(list 'quote %) args)))))\n355\t\n356\t\n357\t(deftest test-oracle-slice3-destructuring-anchors\n358\t  (testing \"syntax/top-assumption: A (upstream) and C (yang.clojure on the VM) agree\"\n359\t    (doseq [t ['(Π [x :type] x)\n360\t               '(Π [y [:ref A]] (Π [z :type] z))\n361\t               'x\n362\t               '(λ [x :type] x)\n363\t               nil]]\n364\t      (let [a ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.syntax/top-assumption) t)\n365\t            c (run-with-deps 'latte_kernel.syntax '[prod? top-assumption]\n366\t                             'top-assumption [t])]\n367\t        (is (= a c) (str \"top-assumption on \" (pr-str t)))))\n368\t    (testing \"the anchor genuinely uses a nested destructuring let\"\n369\t      (is (some (fn [f]\n370\t                  (and (seq? f) (= 'let (first f))\n371\t                       (some vector? (take-nth 2 (second f)))))\n372\t                (tree-seq coll? seq\n373\t                          (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.syntax 'top-assumption]))))))\n374\t  (testing \"defenv/register-definition is multi-arity: rejected explicitly, never half-compiled\"\n375\t    (let [form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.defenv 'register-definition])]\n376\t      (is (contains? (classify-form form) :multi-arity))\n377\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo #\"Multi-arity\"\n378\t            (yang/compile-program [form]))))))\n379\t\n380\t\n381\t;; =============================================================================\n382\t;; Slice 3b: multi-arity through the argument-vector convention\n383\t;; =============================================================================\n384\t\n385\t(defn- run-av-with-deps\n386\t  \"run-with-deps through the argument-vector convention.\"\n387\t  [ns-sym dep-names fname args]\n388\t  (let [forms (mapv #(get top-forms [ns-sym %]) dep-names)]\n389\t    (run-on-vm forms (list* fname (map #(list 'quote %) args)))))\n390\t\n391\t\n392\t(deftest test-oracle-slice3b-multi-arity\n393\t  (let [register (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition)\n394\t        c-register (fn [& args]\n395\t                     (run-av-with-deps 'latte_kernel.defenv '[register-definition]\n396\t                                       'register-definition (vec args)))\n397\t        rdef {:name 'f, :arity 1}\n398\t        env [{'g {:name 'g}} {'h {:name 'h}}]]\n399\t    (testing \"defenv/register-definition: both arities, both placements, A = C\"\n400\t      (doseq [args [[env rdef]\n401\t                    [env rdef false]\n402\t                    [env rdef true]\n403\t                    [[{} {}] rdef]\n404\t                    [[{} {}] rdef true]]]\n405\t        (is (= (apply register args) (apply c-register args))\n406\t            (pr-str args)))\n407\t      (is (= [{'g {:name 'g}, 'f rdef} {'h {:name 'h}}] (c-register env rdef))\n408\t          \"the two-argument form registers globally\")\n409\t      (is (= [{'g {:name 'g}} {'h {:name 'h}, 'f rdef}] (c-register env rdef true))\n410\t          \"the three-argument form with local? true registers locally\"))\n411\t    (testing \"a wrong-count call is a rejection fixture\"\n412\t      (doseq [args [[env] [] [env rdef true :extra]]]\n413\t        (is (= :arity\n414\t               (try (apply c-register args) nil\n415\t                    (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n416\t                      (:yin.vm.data/reason (ex-data e)))))\n417\t            (pr-str args)))))\n418\t  (testing \"single-arity anchors still pass through the convention\"\n419\t    (doseq [t ['(Π [x :type] x) '(Π [y [:ref A]] (Π [z :type] z)) 'x nil]]\n420\t      (is (= ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.syntax/top-assumption) t)\n421\t             (run-av-with-deps 'latte_kernel.syntax '[prod? top-assumption]\n422\t                               'top-assumption [t]))\n423\t          (str \"top-assumption on \" (pr-str t))))\n424\t    (is (= ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/mkenv) [])\n425\t           (run-av-with-deps 'latte_kernel.defenv '[mkenv] 'mkenv [[]])))))\n426\t\n427\t\n428\t;; =============================================================================\n429\t;; Slice 4: loop/recur anchors, upstream A leg against the compiled C leg\n430\t;; =============================================================================\n431\t\n432\t(defn- agree\n433\t  \"Run upstream `qsym` and the C leg (`deps` first, then the function) on\n434\t   each argument vector and assert A = C.\"\n435\t  [qsym ns-sym deps arg-lists]\n436\t  (let [a-fn (upstream-fn qsym)\n437\t        fname (symbol (name qsym))]\n438\t    (doseq [args arg-lists]\n439\t      (is (= (apply a-fn args)\n440\t             (run-with-deps ns-sym deps fname args))\n441\t          (str fname \" on \" (pr-str args))))))\n442\t\n443\t\n444\t(deftest test-oracle-slice4-loop-anchors\n445\t  (testing \"utils/vconcat and utils/vcons: empty and non-empty, both orders\"\n446\t    (agree 'latte-kernel.utils/vconcat 'latte_kernel.utils '[vconcat]\n447\t           [[[] []] [[] [1 2]] [[1 2] []] [[1 2] [3 4]] [[3 4] [1 2]] ['[[a]] '[[b] c]]])\n448\t    (agree 'latte-kernel.utils/vcons 'latte_kernel.utils '[vconcat vcons]\n449\t           [[1 []] [1 [2 3]] [[0] [1]] ['x ['y 'z]]]))\n450\t  (testing \"typing/ctx-fetch: found, not found, empty context, shadowed\"\n451\t    (agree 'latte-kernel.typing/ctx-fetch 'latte_kernel.typing '[ctx-fetch]\n452\t           [['[[x A] [y B]] 'x]\n453\t            ['[[x A] [y B]] 'y]\n454\t            ['[[x A] [y B]] 'z]\n455\t            ['[] 'x]\n456\t            [nil 'x]\n457\t            ['[[x A] [y B] [x C]] 'x]\n458\t            ['[[y B] [x C] [x A]] 'x]\n459\t            ['[[x [:ref A]]] 'x]]))\n460\t  (testing \"syntax/binderify: zero, one and three bindings\"\n461\t    (agree 'latte-kernel.syntax/binderify 'latte_kernel.syntax '[binderify]\n462\t           [['λ [] 'body]\n463\t            ['λ '[[x :type]] 'body]\n464\t            ['Π '[[x :type] [y [:ref A]] [z :type]] '(f x y z)]]))\n465\t  (testing \"syntax/appify: zero, one and three arguments\"\n466\t    (agree 'latte-kernel.syntax/appify 'latte_kernel.syntax '[appify]\n467\t           [['f []] ['f '[a]] ['f '[a b c]] ['[g h] '[a [b c]]]]))\n468\t  (testing \"syntax/assumptions: nil, non-product, one and two nested products\"\n469\t    (agree 'latte-kernel.syntax/assumptions 'latte_kernel.syntax\n470\t           '[prod? top-assumption assumptions]\n471\t           [[nil]\n472\t            ['x]\n473\t            ['(λ [x :type] x)]\n474\t            ['(Π [x :type] x)]\n475\t            ['(Π [x :type] (Π [y [:ref A]] z))]\n476\t            ['(Π [x :type] (Π [y [:ref A]] (Π [z :type] z)))]])))\n477\t\n478\t\n479\t(deftest test-oracle-slice4-mk-fresh\n480\t  (let [a-fn (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.syntax/mk-fresh)\n481\t        form (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.syntax 'mk-fresh])\n482\t        c-fn (fn [& args]\n483\t               (run-on-vm [form] (list* 'mk-fresh (map #(list 'quote %) args))))]\n484\t    (testing \"the source carries a multi-arity branch that recurs\"\n485\t      (let [source (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.syntax 'mk-fresh])]\n486\t        (is (= 2 (count (filter #(and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) source))))\n487\t        (is (contains? (set (walk-symbols source)) 'recur))))\n488\t    (testing \"suffix levels 0 to 5 through collisions, A = C\"\n489\t      (let [forbids [#{}\n490\t                     '#{x}\n491\t                     '#{x x'}\n492\t                     '#{x x' x''}\n493\t                     '#{x x' x'' x'''}\n494\t                     '#{x x' x'' x''' x-4}\n495\t                     '#{x x' x'' x''' x-4 x-5}\n496\t                     '#{y}]]\n497\t        (doseq [forbid forbids]\n498\t          (is (= (a-fn 'x forbid) (c-fn 'x forbid)) (pr-str forbid))\n499\t          (doseq [level (range 6)]\n500\t            (is (= (a-fn 'x level forbid) (c-fn 'x level forbid))\n501\t                (str \"level \" level \" \" (pr-str forbid)))))\n502\t        (is (= 'x-5 (c-fn 'x '#{x x' x'' x''' x-4})))\n503\t        (is (= 'x (c-fn 'x #{})))))))\n504\t\n505\t\n506\t;; =============================================================================\n507\t;; Slice 5: outcome channel beside the value channel\n508\t;; =============================================================================\n509\t\n510\t(defn- desugar\n511\t  \"Drop corpus namespace aliases and normalize reader-generated fn* to fn.\n512\t   Only finite utils/zip admits eager lazy-seq adaptation; cond and if-let\n513\t   are compiler forms.\"\n514\t  [form]\n515\t  (let [finite-zip? (and (seq? form) (= 'defn (first form)) (= 'zip (second form)))]\n516\t    (walk/postwalk\n517\t      (fn [f]\n518\t        (cond\n519\t          (and (seq? f) (= 'lazy-seq (first f)))\n520\t          (if finite-zip? (second f)\n521\t              (throw (ex-info \"Only finite utils/zip admits eager lazy-seq adaptation\" {})))\n522\t          (= f 'fn*) 'fn\n523\t          (and (symbol? f) (#{\"stx\" \"defenv\" \"nbe\" \"norm\" \"utils\" \"set\"} (namespace f)))\n524\t          (symbol (name f))\n525\t          :else f))\n526\t      form)))\n527\t\n528\t\n529\t(defn- a-leg\n530\t  \"The upstream result as a value or a caught ex-info (message and data; a\n531\t   stack trace is never compared).\"\n532\t  [f args]\n533\t  (try {:value (let [v (apply f args)] (if (seq? v) (doall v) v))}\n534\t       (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n535\t         {:thrown {:message (ex-message e), :data (ex-data e)}})))\n536\t\n537\t\n538\t(defn- agrees?\n539\t  \"The outcome `c` is the A leg's value as a success or its exception as the\n540\t   portable error map.\"\n541\t  [a c]\n542\t  (if (contains? a :value)\n543\t    (= [:yin.k/ok (:value a)] c)\n544\t    (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message (get-in a [:thrown :message])\n545\t                      :yin.k/data (get-in a [:thrown :data])}]\n546\t       c)))\n547\t\n548\t\n549\t(defn- ab\n550\t  \"Run upstream `qsym` and the outcome-model C leg (`deps` first) on `args`;\n551\t   returns [a c] and asserts they agree.\"\n552\t  [qsym ns-sym deps args]\n553\t  (let [fname (symbol (name qsym))\n554\t        forms (mapv #(desugar (get top-forms (if (vector? %) % [ns-sym %]))) deps)\n555\t        a (a-leg (upstream-fn qsym) args)\n556\t        c (run-outcome forms (list* fname (map #(list 'quote %) args)))]\n557\t    (is (agrees? a c) (str fname \" \" (pr-str args) \" A=\" (pr-str a) \" C=\" (pr-str c)))\n558\t    [a c]))\n559\t\n560\t\n561\t(deftest test-oracle-slice5-throw-site-fixtures\n562\t  (testing \"utils/safe-get: success and failure\"\n563\t    (let [[a1 _] (ab 'latte-kernel.utils/safe-get 'latte_kernel.utils '[safe-get] ['{:a 1} :a])\n564\t          [a2 c2] (ab 'latte-kernel.utils/safe-get 'latte_kernel.utils '[safe-get] ['{:a 1} :b])]\n565\t      (is (contains? a1 :value))\n566\t      (is (= \"No such value in collection\" (get-in a2 [:thrown :message])))\n567\t      (is (= :yin.k/error (first c2)))))\n568\t  (testing \"utils/zip: even length succeeds, odd length throws\"\n569\t    (doseq [s ['(a b c d) '() '(a b)]]\n570\t      (ab 'latte-kernel.utils/zip 'latte_kernel.utils '[zip] [s]))\n571\t    (let [[a _] (ab 'latte-kernel.utils/zip 'latte_kernel.utils '[zip] ['(a b c)])]\n572\t      ;; upstream is lazy: realizing the sequence is what throws\n573\t      (is (or (contains? a :thrown) (nil? (try (doall (:value a)) nil\n574\t                                               (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e e)))))))\n575\t  (testing \"defenv/fetch-definition: the non-symbol, non-var branch throws\"\n576\t    (ab 'latte-kernel.defenv/fetch-definition 'latte_kernel.defenv '[fetch-definition]\n577\t        ['[{} {}] 5])\n578\t    (ab 'latte-kernel.defenv/fetch-definition 'latte_kernel.defenv '[fetch-definition]\n579\t        ['[{} {}] 5 true])\n580\t    (ab 'latte-kernel.defenv/fetch-definition 'latte_kernel.defenv '[fetch-definition]\n581\t        ['[{} {foo {:name foo}}] 'foo]))\n582\t  (testing \"a wrong-count call is the function's OWN arity error, not a count refusal\"\n583\t    (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.vm.data/reason :arity, :yin.k/fn 'fetch-definition, :yin.k/argc 1}]\n584\t           (run-outcome [(desugar (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.defenv 'fetch-definition]))]\n585\t                        '(fetch-definition [{} {}])))))\n586\t  (testing \"norm and nbe delta-reduction: No such definition\"\n587\t    (doseq [[qsym ns-sym args] [['latte-kernel.nbe/delta-reduction 'latte_kernel.nbe\n588\t                                 ['[{} {}] [] '(no-such-definition-xyz)]]\n589\t                                ['latte-kernel.norm/delta-reduction 'latte_kernel.norm\n590\t                                 ['[{} {}] [] '(no-such-definition-xyz)]]]\n591\t            :let [[a c] (ab qsym ns-sym\n592\t                            [['latte_kernel.defenv 'fetch-definition]\n593\t                             ['latte_kernel.syntax 'ref?]\n594\t                             'delta-reduction]\n595\t                            args)]]\n596\t      (is (= \"No such definition\" (get-in a [:thrown :message])) (str qsym))\n597\t      (is (= :yin.k/error (first c))))))\n598\t\n599\t\n600\t;; =============================================================================\n601\t;; Slice 5: unfold-implicit, adapted from typing.cljc:453\n602\t;; =============================================================================\n603\t\n604\t(def ^:private unfold-implicit-adaptation\n605\t  \"The checked-in B-leg source of `typing/unfold-implicit`\n606\t   (test/yang/latte_oracle/unfold_implicit.edn).\"\n607\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/unfold_implicit.edn\"))))\n608\t\n609\t\n610\t(defn- upstream-unfold\n611\t  \"The upstream catch shape over a host implicit fn.\"\n612\t  [implicit-def args]\n613\t  (try [:ok ((:fn implicit-def) args) args]\n614\t       (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n615\t         [:ko (merge {:implicit (:name implicit-def), :msg (ex-message e)} (ex-data e)) nil])))\n616\t\n617\t\n618\t(deftest test-oracle-slice5-unfold-implicit\n619\t  (let [b-leg (fn [fn-form args]\n620\t                (run-outcome [(list 'def 'impl {:name ''imp, :fn fn-form})\n621\t                              unfold-implicit-adaptation]\n622\t                             (list 'unfold-implicit 'impl (list 'quote args))))\n623\t        ok-form '(fn [args] (first args))\n624\t        a-ok {:name 'imp, :fn first}\n625\t        a-throw {:name 'imp, :fn (fn [_] (throw (ex-info \"implicit failed\" {:msg \"data wins\" :extra 1})))}\n626\t        throw-form '(fn [args] (throw (ex-info \"implicit failed\" {:msg \"data wins\", :extra 1})))]\n627\t    (testing \"success: [:ok value args]\"\n628\t      (is (= (upstream-unfold a-ok '[7 8])\n629\t             (second (b-leg ok-form '[7 8])))))\n630\t    (testing \"failure: error outcome consumed, data overrides :msg, result is [:ko ... nil]\"\n631\t      (is (= (upstream-unfold a-throw '[7])\n632\t             (second (b-leg throw-form '[7]))))\n633\t      (is (= [:ko {:implicit 'imp, :msg \"data wins\", :extra 1} nil]\n634\t             (second (b-leg throw-form '[7])))))))\n635\t\n636\t\n637\t;; =============================================================================\n638\t;; Slice 5: the throw-site inventory\n639\t;; =============================================================================\n640\t\n641\t(defn- throw-forms\n642\t  [form]\n643\t  (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'throw (first %))) (tree-seq coll? seq form)))\n644\t\n645\t\n646\t(defn- throw-symbol-count\n647\t  \"Every `throw` symbol in the manifest's top-level forms.\"\n648\t  []\n649\t  (count (for [{:keys [ns name]} manifest\n650\t               s (tree-seq coll? seq (get top-forms [ns name]))\n651\t               :when (= 'throw s)]\n652\t           s)))\n653\t\n654\t\n655\t(def ^:private fixture-sites\n656\t  \"[ns fn message-fragment] of the sites slice 5 fixes with an A/B fixture.\"\n657\t  #{['latte_kernel.utils 'safe-get \"No such value\"]\n658\t    ['latte_kernel.utils 'zip \"odd number\"]\n659\t    ['latte_kernel.defenv 'fetch-definition \"Cannot fetch\"]\n660\t    ['latte_kernel.norm 'delta-reduction \"No such definition\"]\n661\t    ['latte_kernel.nbe 'delta-reduction \"No such definition\"]})\n662\t\n663\t\n664\t(defn- disposition\n665\t  [ns-sym fname message]\n666\t  (if (some (fn [[n f frag]]\n667\t              (and (= n ns-sym) (= f fname) message (str/includes? message frag)))\n668\t            fixture-sites)\n669\t    {:disposition :fixture}\n670\t    {:disposition :deferred\n671\t     :to (str \"the slice that admits \" ns-sym \"/\" fname)}))\n672\t\n673\t\n674\t(defn- throw-site-rows\n675\t  []\n676\t  (vec (for [{:keys [ns name]} manifest\n677\t             t (throw-forms (get top-forms [ns name]))\n678\t             :let [message (first (filter string? (tree-seq coll? seq t)))]]\n679\t         (merge {:ns ns, :fn name, :line (:line (meta t)), :message message}\n680\t                (disposition ns name message)))))\n681\t\n682\t\n683\t(def ^:private throw-site-table\n684\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn\"))))\n685\t\n686\t\n687\t(deftest test-throw-site-inventory\n688\t  (testing \"the checked-in table has one row per throw symbol in the manifest forms\"\n689\t    (is (= (throw-symbol-count) (count throw-site-table)))\n690\t    (is (= (throw-site-rows) throw-site-table)\n691\t        \"regenerate with: clj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main (corpus or disposition change)\"))\n692\t  (testing \"every row has a disposition\"\n693\t    (is (every? #{:fixture :deferred :excluded} (map :disposition throw-site-table)))\n694\t    (is (every? #(or (not= :deferred (:disposition %)) (:to %)) throw-site-table)))\n695\t  (testing \"slice 5 assigns the fixtures the design names\"\n696\t    (let [fixtures (filter #(= :fixture (:disposition %)) throw-site-table)]\n697\t      (is (= 5 (count fixtures)))\n698\t      (is (= #{['latte_kernel.utils 'safe-get] ['latte_kernel.utils 'zip]\n699\t               ['latte_kernel.defenv 'fetch-definition] ['latte_kernel.norm 'delta-reduction]\n700\t               ['latte_kernel.nbe 'delta-reduction]}\n701\t             (set (map (juxt :ns :fn) fixtures)))))))\n702\t\n703\t\n704\t;; =============================================================================\n705\t;; Slice 7: per-arm case fixtures\n706\t;; =============================================================================\n707\t;;\n708\t;; The corpus has six `case` sites. Each is walked, every clause's constants are\n709\t;; extracted, and a synthetic dispatch (one arm per clause, each returning its\n710\t;; arm index, plus the site's default) runs on the host (A leg) and through\n711\t;; yang.clojure on the VM (C leg). The extracted table is checked in\n712\t;; (test/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn) and regenerated, with the throw-site\n713\t;; table, by src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj.\n714\t\n715\t(defn- case-forms\n716\t  [form]\n717\t  (filter #(and (seq? %) (= 'case (first %))) (tree-seq coll? seq form)))\n718\t\n719\t\n720\t(defn- case-clause-constants\n721\t  \"The constants of one clause key: a list groups them, anything else is one.\"\n722\t  [k]\n723\t  (if (seq? k) (vec k) [k]))\n724\t\n725\t\n726\t(defn- case-arm-rows\n727\t  \"One row per `case` site in the manifest forms: the clause constants of each\n728\t   arm, and whether the site has a default.\"\n729\t  []\n730\t  (vec (for [{:keys [ns name]} manifest\n731\t             c (case-forms (get top-forms [ns name]))\n732\t             :let [clauses (drop 2 c)]]\n733\t         {:ns ns, :fn name, :line (:line (meta c))\n734\t          :default? (odd? (count clauses))\n735\t          :arms (vec (map-indexed (fn [i [k _]] {:arm i, :constants (case-clause-constants k)})\n736\t                                  (partition 2 clauses)))})))\n737\t\n738\t\n739\t(def ^:private case-arm-table\n740\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn\"))))\n741\t\n742\t\n743\t(def ^:private unmatched\n744\t  \"An input no corpus clause names.\"\n745\t  :yang.latte-oracle/unmatched)\n746\t\n747\t\n748\t(defn- dispatch-clauses\n749\t  \"The clauses of a synthetic `case`: each arm's constants as one group\n750\t   returning the arm index, then the default `:default` when the site has one.\"\n751\t  [{:keys [arms default?]}]\n752\t  (concat (mapcat (fn [{:keys [arm constants]}] [(apply list constants) arm]) arms)\n753\t          (when default? [:default])))\n754\t\n755\t\n756\t(defn- a-dispatch\n757\t  \"The host `case` over the same clauses, applied to `input`; ::no-match when\n758\t   no clause (and no default) takes it.\"\n759\t  [row input]\n760\t  (try ((eval (list 'fn '[e] (list* 'case 'e (dispatch-clauses row)))) input)\n761\t       (catch IllegalArgumentException _ ::no-match)))\n762\t\n763\t\n764\t(defn- c-dispatch\n765\t  \"The synthetic dispatch compiled through yang.clojure and run on the VM:\n766\t   the outcomes of calling it on each of `inputs`, in order.\"\n767\t  [row inputs]\n768\t  (let [dispatch (list 'defn 'dispatch '[e] (list* 'case 'e (dispatch-clauses row)))]\n769\t    (mapv (fn [input] (run-outcome [dispatch] (list 'dispatch (list 'quote input)))) inputs)))\n770\t\n771\t\n772\t(deftest test-case-arm-table\n773\t  (testing \"the checked-in table is the walk of the corpus's case sites\"\n774\t    (is (= 6 (count case-arm-table)))\n775\t    (is (= (case-arm-rows) case-arm-table)\n776\t        \"regenerate with: clj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\")\n777\t    (is (= #{['latte_kernel.norm 'beta-red] ['latte_kernel.norm 'beta-delta-normalize]\n778\t             ['latte_kernel.proof 'elab-proof] ['latte_kernel.proof 'elab-proof-step]\n779\t             ['latte_kernel.typing 'type-of-term] ['latte_kernel.syntax 'mk-fresh]}\n780\t           (set (map (juxt :ns :fn) case-arm-table)))))\n781\t  (testing \"every arm of every site has constants, and arms never share one\"\n782\t    (doseq [{:keys [arms] :as row} case-arm-table\n783\t            :let [constants (mapcat :constants arms)]]\n784\t      (is (every? (comp seq :constants) arms) (pr-str (:fn row)))\n785\t      (is (apply distinct? constants) (pr-str (:fn row))))))\n786\t\n787\t\n788\t(deftest test-case-arm-fixtures\n789\t  (doseq [{:keys [arms default?] :as row} case-arm-table\n790\t          :let [label (str (:ns row) \"/\" (:fn row) \" line \" (:line row))]]\n791\t    (testing label\n792\t      (testing \"every constant of every arm dispatches to its own arm, A = C\"\n793\t        (let [inputs (mapcat :constants arms)\n794\t              expected (mapcat (fn [{:keys [arm constants]}] (repeat (count constants) arm)) arms)]\n795\t          (is (= expected (map #(a-dispatch row %) inputs)) \"host case\")\n796\t          (is (= (map (fn [e] [:yin.k/ok e]) expected) (c-dispatch row inputs)) \"VM\")))\n797\t      (testing \"an input no clause names takes the default, or fails without one\"\n798\t        (let [[c] (c-dispatch row [unmatched])]\n799\t          (if default?\n800\t            (do (is (= :default (a-dispatch row unmatched)))\n801\t                (is (= [:yin.k/ok :default] c)))\n802\t            (do (is (= ::no-match (a-dispatch row unmatched)))\n803\t                (is (= :yin.k/error (first c)))\n804\t                (is (= \"No matching clause in case\" (:yin.k/message (second c)))))))))))\n805\t\n806\t\n807\t;; =============================================================================\n808\t;; Slice 7: upstream higher-order and syntax anchors, both VM lanes\n809\t;; =============================================================================\n810\t\n811\t(def ^:private slice7-anchors\n812\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice7_anchors.edn\"))))\n813\t\n814\t\n815\t(deftest test-oracle-slice7-library-anchors\n816\t  (let [{:keys [dependency-groups anchors]} slice7-anchors]\n817\t    (is (= '#{map-with vremove term-reduce free-vars vars subst alpha-norm readable-term}\n818\t           (set (map :fn anchors))))\n819\t    (doseq [{ns-sym :ns fname :fn :keys [groups deps args]} anchors\n820\t            :let [names (distinct (concat (mapcat dependency-groups groups) deps))\n821\t                  forms (mapv #(desugar (get top-forms [ns-sym %])) names)\n822\t                  qsym (symbol (str (str/replace (str ns-sym) \"_\" \"-\") \"/\" fname))]]\n823\t      (testing (str qsym)\n824\t        (is (every? some? forms) \"every declared dependency exists in pinned upstream\")\n825\t        (doseq [arg-forms args\n826\t                :let [host-args (mapv eval arg-forms)\n827\t                      a (a-leg (upstream-fn qsym) host-args)\n828\t                      c (run-outcome forms (list* fname arg-forms))]]\n829\t          (is (agrees? a c) (str qsym \" \" (pr-str arg-forms)\n830\t                                 \" A=\" (pr-str a) \" C=\" (pr-str c)))\n831\t          (when (contains? a :value)\n832\t            (is (= (result-shape (:value a)) (result-shape (second c)))\n833\t                \"value equality also preserves nested metadata and collection shape\")))))))\n834\t\n835\t\n836\t(deftest test-oracle-slice7-finite-zip\n837\t  ;; The pinned corpus has one consumer, proof/compile-proof's :assume arm:\n838\t  ;; it loops over all pairs to build declarations, then reverses all pairs\n839\t  ;; to build discharges. It requires finite, fully consumed inputs; it does\n840\t  ;; not catch zip failures or depend on partial realization/error timing.\n841\t  (let [source (get top-forms ['latte_kernel.utils 'zip])\n842\t        forms [(desugar source)]]\n843\t    (is (thrown-with-msg? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo #\"Only finite utils/zip\"\n844\t          (desugar '(defn other\n845\t                      [s]\n846\t                      (lazy-seq s)))))\n847\t    (is (= 1 (count (filter #(= 'lazy-seq %) (walk-symbols source))))\n848\t        \"zip is the single explicit eager lazy-seq adaptation\")\n849\t    (doseq [input [nil [] '() '[a A] '(a A b B c C) '[a A b]]\n850\t            :let [a (a-leg (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.utils/zip) [input])\n851\t                  c (run-outcome forms (list 'zip (list 'quote input)))]]\n852\t      (is (agrees? a c) (str \"fully realized finite zip \" (pr-str input))))\n853\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok [true 2 '[a A] '([b B]) '(:front [a A] [b B])]]\n854\t           (run-outcome forms\n855\t                        '(let [s (zip '(a A b B))]\n856\t                           [(seq? s) (count s) (first s) (rest s) (conj s :front)]))))))\n857\t\n858\t\n859\t;; =============================================================================\n860\t;; Slice 8: immutable kernel state and explicit extension installation\n861\t;; =============================================================================\n862\t\n863\t(def ^:private context-source\n864\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/context.edn\"))))\n865\t\n866\t\n867\t(defn- context-upstream-form\n868\t  \"Keep the upstream implementation, changing only the environment boundary\n869\t   and module-local names. Both delta implementations read the SAME binding.\"\n870\t  [ns-sym fname]\n871\t  (let [renames (if (#{'latte_kernel.nbe 'latte_kernel.norm} ns-sym)\n872\t                  {'delta-reduction (symbol (str (last (str/split (clojure.core/name ns-sym) #\"\\.\")) \"-delta\"))\n873\t                   'instantiate-def (symbol (str (last (str/split (clojure.core/name ns-sym) #\"\\.\")) \"-instantiate\"))}\n874\t                  {})]\n875\t    (walk/postwalk\n876\t      (fn [x]\n877\t        (cond\n878\t          (and (seq? x) (#{'deref 'clojure.core/deref} (first x))\n879\t               (= '+unfold-implicit+ (second x))) '(:unfold-implicit def-env)\n880\t          (contains? '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\n881\t                       ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\n882\t          (get '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\n883\t                 ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\n884\t          (symbol? x) (get renames x x)\n885\t          :else x))\n886\t      (desugar (get top-forms [ns-sym fname])))))\n887\t\n888\t\n889\t(def ^:private context-forms\n890\t  (into context-source\n891\t        (concat\n892\t          (map #(context-upstream-form 'latte_kernel.syntax %)\n893\t               '[kind? type? variable? binder? lambda? prod? app? ascription? ref?\n894\t                 host-constant? binderify free-vars vars mk-fresh subst- rebinder subst])\n895\t          (map #(context-upstream-form 'latte_kernel.nbe %) '[instantiate-def delta-reduction])\n896\t          (map #(context-upstream-form 'latte_kernel.norm %) '[instantiate-def delta-reduction])\n897\t          [(context-upstream-form 'latte_kernel.proof 'elab-proof)]\n898\t          (map #(context-upstream-form 'latte_kernel.unparser %)\n899\t               '[unparse-term-once unparse-term-rec prod-impl-unparser])\n900\t          '[(defn unparse\n901\t              [kernel term]\n902\t              (first (unparse-term-rec (:unparser-registry kernel) (unparser-order kernel) term)))\n903\t            (defn install-fundamental-unparsers\n904\t              [kernel]\n905\t              (register-unparser kernel :fundamental :prod-impl prod-impl-unparser))])))\n906\t\n907\t\n908\t(defn- context-for\n909\t  \"The transitive source dependency closure, preserving upstream order.\"\n910\t  [program]\n911\t  (let [by-name (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) context-forms)\n912\t        mentions (fn [form] (filter #(contains? by-name %) (walk-symbols form)))\n913\t        needed (loop [todo (seq (mapcat mentions program)) seen #{}]\n914\t                 (if-let [n (first todo)]\n915\t                   (if (contains? seen n)\n916\t                     (recur (next todo) seen)\n917\t                     (recur (concat (next todo) (mentions (get by-name n))) (conj seen n)))\n918\t                   seen))]\n919\t    (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) context-forms)))\n920\t\n921\t\n922\t(defn- context-host-form\n923\t  \"B is ordinary Clojure over the checked-in adaptation. The sole guest\n924\t   outcome intrinsic becomes the equivalent host catch; data primitives and\n925\t   deterministic gensym retain exactly their portable contracts.\"\n926\t  [form]\n927\t  (walk/postwalk\n928\t    (fn [x]\n929\t      (cond\n930\t        (and (seq? x) (= 'yin.k/outcome-of (first x)))\n931\t        `(try [:yin.k/ok ~(second x)]\n932\t              (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e#\n933\t                [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message (ex-message e#) :yin.k/data (ex-data e#)}]))\n934\t        (and (seq? x) (= 'gensym (first x)))\n935\t        (let [[_ prefix n] x]\n936\t          (list 'let ['prefix prefix 'n n]\n937\t                '(if (map? prefix)\n938\t                   [(symbol (str \"G__\" n (:counter prefix)))\n939\t                    (assoc prefix :counter (inc (:counter prefix)))]\n940\t                   (symbol (str prefix n)))))\n941\t        (and (seq? x) (= 'fresh-symbol (first x)))\n942\t        (let [[_ supply prefix] x]\n943\t          (list 'let ['supply supply]\n944\t                (list 'vector (list 'symbol (list 'str \"G__\" prefix '(:counter supply)))\n945\t                      '(assoc supply :counter (inc (:counter supply))))))\n946\t        (= x 'data/dissoc) 'clojure.core/dissoc\n947\t        :else x))\n948\t    form))\n949\t\n950\t\n951\t(defn- context-b\n952\t  [forms call]\n953\t  (let [ns-sym (gensym \"latte-context-b-\")\n954\t        sandbox (create-ns ns-sym)]\n955\t    (try\n956\t      (binding [*ns* sandbox]\n957\t        (refer 'clojure.core)\n958\t        (require '[clojure.set :refer [union difference]])\n959\t        (eval '(declare subst- rebinder subst))\n960\t        (doseq [form (concat (context-for (conj forms call)) forms)] (eval (context-host-form form)))\n961\t        (a-leg (eval (context-host-form (list 'fn [] call))) []))\n962\t      (finally (remove-ns ns-sym)))))\n963\t\n964\t\n965\t(defn- context-bc\n966\t  [forms call]\n967\t  (let [b (context-b forms call)\n968\t        c (run-outcome (into (context-for (conj forms call)) forms) call (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) true)]\n969\t    (is (agrees? b c) (str \"context B/C \" (pr-str call) \" B=\" (pr-str b) \" C=\" (pr-str c)))\n970\t    (when (contains? b :value)\n971\t      (is (= (result-shape (:value b)) (result-shape (second c)))\n972\t          \"B/C preserve collection families and domain metadata\"))\n973\t    c))\n974\t\n975\t\n976\t(def ^:private initial-context\n977\t  '(kernel-context [{} {}] definition-opacity missing-unfold-implicit))\n978\t\n979\t\n980\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-context-isolation\n981\t  (let [call (walk/postwalk-replace\n982\t               {'INITIAL initial-context}\n983\t               '(let [k0 INITIAL other INITIAL\n984\t                      d (->Definition 'd [] 0 'body #{} 'T {})\n985\t                      k1 (register-definition k0 d)\n986\t                      k2 (register-definition k1 (->Axiom 'a [] 0 'T) true)\n987\t                      [fresh k3] (fresh-name k2 \"fresh\")\n988\t                      [fresh2 k4] (fresh-name k3 \"fresh\")]\n989\t                  [(fetch-definition k0 'd) (fetch-definition other 'd)\n990\t                   (fetch-definition k1 'd) (fetch-definition k2 'a true)\n991\t                   (fetch-definition k2 'd true) (qualify-def k2 'd)\n992\t                   fresh fresh2 (:fresh k0) (:fresh k2) (:fresh k3) (:fresh k4)]))\n993\t        [_ result] (context-bc [] call)]\n994\t    (is (= (first result) (second result)))\n995\t    (is (= [:ko {:msg \"No such (global) definition\" :def 'd}] (first result)))\n996\t    (is (= ['fresh0 'fresh1 0 0 1 2] (subvec result 6))))\n997\t  (testing \"no namespace fallback, even when a host name resolves\"\n998\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok [:ko {:msg \"No such (global) definition\" :def 'clojure.core/map}]]\n999\t           (context-bc [] (list 'fetch-definition initial-context ''clojure.core/map)))))\n1000\t  (testing \"missing installations and bad names are explicit outcomes\"\n1001\t    (doseq [call [(list 'qualify-def initial-context ''missing)\n1002\t                  (list 'fetch-definition initial-context 5)\n1003\t                  '(let [k (kernel-context [{} {}] missing-opacity-policy missing-unfold-implicit)\n1004\t                         k (register-definition k (->Definition 'd [] 0 'body #{} 'T {}))]\n1005\t                     (elab-opaque k '[d]))]]\n1006\t      (is (= :yin.k/error (first (context-bc [] call)))))))\n1007\t\n1008\t\n1009\t(defn- upstream-record-data\n1010\t  \"Declare only the five approved record representations equivalent. Kind\n1011\t   and every field survive normalization; arbitrary host objects do not.\"\n1012\t  [x]\n1013\t  (let [predicates [['latte-kernel.defenv/definition? :definition]\n1014\t                    ['latte-kernel.defenv/theorem? :theorem]\n1015\t                    ['latte-kernel.defenv/axiom? :axiom]\n1016\t                    ['latte-kernel.defenv/notation? :notation]\n1017\t                    ['latte-kernel.defenv/implicit? :implicit]]]\n1018\t    (walk/postwalk\n1019\t      (fn [v]\n1020\t        (if-let [kind (some (fn [[pred kind]] (when ((upstream-fn pred) v) kind)) predicates)]\n1021\t          (assoc (into {} v) :latte/kind kind)\n1022\t          v))\n1023\t      x)))\n1024\t\n1025\t\n1026\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-definition-kinds-and-delta\n1027\t  (doseq [[ctor args term-args] [['->Definition '['d [] 0 'body #{} 'T {}]]\n1028\t                                 ['->Definition '['opaque [] 0 'body #{} 'T {:opaque true}]]\n1029\t                                 ['->Axiom '['a [] 0 'T]]\n1030\t                                 ['->Theorem '['proved [] 0 'T 'proof]]\n1031\t                                 ['->Theorem '['unproved [] 0 'T nil]]\n1032\t                                 ['->Definition '['empty [] 0 nil #{} 'T {}]]\n1033\t                                 ['->Definition '['param '[[x T]] 1 'x #{} 'T {}] ['arg]]\n1034\t                                 ['->Definition '['partial '[[x T]] 1 'x #{} 'T {}]]\n1035\t                                 ['->Definition '['too-many [] 0 'body #{} 'T {}] ['arg]]]\n1036\t          ns-sym ['latte_kernel.nbe 'latte_kernel.norm]\n1037\t          :let [record (apply (upstream-fn (symbol \"latte-kernel.defenv\" (name ctor))) (map eval args))\n1038\t                name (:name record)\n1039\t                env ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition) [{} {}] record)\n1040\t                a (upstream-record-data\n1041\t                    (a-leg (upstream-fn (symbol (str/replace (str ns-sym) \"_\" \"-\") \"delta-reduction\"))\n1042\t                           [env [] (apply list name term-args)]))\n1043\t                call (list 'let ['k (list 'register-definition initial-context (cons ctor args))]\n1044\t                           (list (symbol (str (last (str/split (clojure.core/name ns-sym) #\"\\.\")) \"-delta\")) 'k [] (list 'quote (apply list name term-args))))\n1045\t                c (context-bc [] call)]]\n1046\t    (is (agrees? a c) (str \"A/B/C \" ctor \" \" name \" \" ns-sym)))\n1047\t  (testing \"all five explicit predicates distinguish plain maps and each other\"\n1048\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok [true true true true true false false]]\n1049\t           (context-bc []\n1050\t                       '(let [n (->Notation 'n (fn [x] x)) i (->Implicit 'i (fn [k ctx x] x))]\n1051\t                          [(definition? (->Definition 'd [] 0 'b #{} 'T {}))\n1052\t                           (theorem? (->Theorem 't [] 0 'T nil)) (axiom? (->Axiom 'a [] 0 'T))\n1053\t                           (notation? n) (implicit? i) (definition? n) (latte-definition? {})])))))\n1054\t  (testing \"notation extension functions execute inside the guest\"\n1055\t    (let [a ((:notation-fn ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Notation) 'n (fn [x] ['expanded x]))) 7)]\n1056\t      (is (= [:yin.k/ok a]\n1057\t             (context-bc [] '(let [n (->Notation 'n (fn [x] ['expanded x]))]\n1058\t                               ((:notation-fn n) 7))))))))\n1059\t\n1060\t\n1061\t(def ^:private slice8-sequences\n1062\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice8_sequences.edn\"))))\n1063\t\n1064\t\n1065\t(def ^:private registry-replay\n1066\t  '[(defn registry-snapshot\n1067\t      [k]\n1068\t      (let [r (:unparser-registry k)]\n1069\t        [(:fundamental r) (:standard r) (:user r) (into #{} (keys (:unparsers r)))\n1070\t         (unparse k 'x)]))\n1071\t    (defn replay-registry\n1072\t      [k operations]\n1073\t      (loop [k k operations operations snapshots [(registry-snapshot k)]]\n1074\t        (if (seq operations)\n1075\t          (let [[op a b c] (first operations)\n1076\t                k (case op\n1077\t                    :register (register-unparser k a b c)\n1078\t                    :register-default (register-unparser k a b)\n1079\t                    :unregister (unregister-unparser k a))]\n1080\t            (recur k (rest operations) (conj snapshots (registry-snapshot k))))\n1081\t          snapshots)))])\n1082\t\n1083\t\n1084\t(defn- a-registry-sequence\n1085\t  [operations]\n1086\t  (let [registry-var (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/+unparser-registry+)\n1087\t        initial {:fundamental [] :standard [] :user [] :unparsers {}}]\n1088\t    (with-redefs-fn {registry-var (atom initial)}\n1089\t      (fn []\n1090\t        (let [snapshot (fn []\n1091\t                         (let [r @@registry-var]\n1092\t                           [(:fundamental r) (:standard r) (:user r) (set (keys (:unparsers r)))\n1093\t                            ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse) 'x)]))]\n1094\t          (reduce (fn [snapshots [op a b c]]\n1095\t                    (case op\n1096\t                      :register ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser!) a b (eval c))\n1097\t                      :register-default ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser!) a (eval b))\n1098\t                      :unregister ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser!) a))\n1099\t                    (conj snapshots (snapshot)))\n1100\t                  [(snapshot)] operations))))))\n1101\t\n1102\t\n1103\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-registry-sequences\n1104\t  (let [ops (:registry slice8-sequences)\n1105\t        a (a-registry-sequence ops)\n1106\t        c (context-bc registry-replay (list 'replay-registry initial-context ops))]\n1107\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok a] c) \"every installation/replacement/removal snapshot matches upstream\"))\n1108\t  (testing \"fundamental installation, category order and recursive unparsing\"\n1109\t    (let [registry-var (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/+unparser-registry+)\n1110\t          a (with-redefs-fn {registry-var (atom {:fundamental [] :standard [] :user [] :unparsers {}})}\n1111\t              (fn []\n1112\t                ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/install-fundamental-unparsers!))\n1113\t                ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse) '(Π [x A] (Π [y B] C)))))]\n1114\t      (is (= [:yin.k/ok a]\n1115\t             (context-bc [] (list 'unparse (list 'install-fundamental-unparsers initial-context)\n1116\t                                  ''(Π [x A] (Π [y B] C))))))))\n1117\t  (testing \"prior contexts retain closure-containing registries\"\n1118\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok ['changed 'x 'x]]\n1119\t           (context-bc []\n1120\t                       (list 'let ['k0 initial-context\n1121\t                                   'k1 '(register-unparser k0 :u (fn [t] ['changed true]))\n1122\t                                   'k2 '(unregister-unparser k1 :u)]\n1123\t                             '[(unparse k1 'x) (unparse k0 'x) (unparse k2 'x)])))))\n1124\t  (doseq [[host-call guest-call] [['latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! '(unregister-unparser K :absent)]\n1125\t                                  ['latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser! '(register-unparser K :bad :x (fn [t] [t false]))]]]\n1126\t    (let [a (if (= host-call 'latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser!)\n1127\t              (a-leg (upstream-fn host-call) [:absent])\n1128\t              (a-leg (upstream-fn host-call) [:bad :x identity]))\n1129\t          c (context-bc [] (walk/postwalk-replace {'K initial-context} guest-call))]\n1130\t      (is (agrees? a c)))))\n1131\t\n1132\t\n1133\t(def ^:private opacity-replay\n1134\t  '[(defn opacity-snapshot\n1135\t      [k]\n1136\t      [(is-opaque? (second (fetch-definition k 'd)))\n1137\t       (nbe-delta k [] '(d)) (norm-delta k [] '(d))])\n1138\t    (defn replay-opacity\n1139\t      [k operations]\n1140\t      (loop [k k operations operations snapshots [(opacity-snapshot k)]]\n1141\t        (if (seq operations)\n1142\t          (let [[status [next-k ctx deps uses]]\n1143\t                (elab-proof-step k [] [] {} (first operations) '[d])]\n1144\t            (recur next-k (rest operations) (conj snapshots (opacity-snapshot next-k))))\n1145\t          snapshots)))])\n1146\t\n1147\t\n1148\t(defn- a-opacity-sequence\n1149\t  [operations]\n1150\t  (let [ns-sym (gensym \"latte-opacity-a-\")\n1151\t        sandbox (create-ns ns-sym)\n1152\t        ddef ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition) 'd [] 0 'body #{} 'T {})\n1153\t        dvar (intern sandbox 'd ddef)\n1154\t        opacity-var (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.proof/+opacity-fn+)]\n1155\t    (try\n1156\t      (binding [*ns* sandbox]\n1157\t        (with-redefs-fn {opacity-var (atom (fn [v flag] (alter-var-root v assoc-in [:opts :opaque] flag)))}\n1158\t          (fn []\n1159\t            (let [snapshot (fn []\n1160\t                             [((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.proof/is-opaque?) @dvar)\n1161\t                              ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.nbe/delta-reduction) [{} {}] [] '(d))\n1162\t                              ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/delta-reduction) [{} {}] [] '(d))])]\n1163\t              (reduce (fn [snapshots op]\n1164\t                        ((upstream-fn (if (= :opaque op) 'latte-kernel.proof/elab-opaque\n1165\t                                          'latte-kernel.proof/elab-transparent)) [{} {}] '[d])\n1166\t                        (conj snapshots (snapshot)))\n1167\t                      [(snapshot)] operations)))))\n1168\t      (finally (remove-ns ns-sym)))))\n1169\t\n1170\t\n1171\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-opacity-propagation\n1172\t  (let [ops (:opacity slice8-sequences)\n1173\t        call (list 'replay-opacity\n1174\t                   (list 'register-definition initial-context '(->Definition 'd [] 0 'body #{} 'T {}))\n1175\t                   ops)]\n1176\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok (a-opacity-sequence ops)] (context-bc opacity-replay call))))\n1177\t  (testing \"local shadowing is updated in place; old/global contexts stay transparent\"\n1178\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok [[nil ['global true]] [true ['(d) false]] [nil ['global true]]]]\n1179\t           (context-bc []\n1180\t                       (list 'let ['base initial-context\n1181\t                                   'global '(register-definition base (->Definition 'd [] 0 'global #{} 'T {}))\n1182\t                                   'local '(register-definition global (->Definition 'd [] 0 'local #{} 'T {}) true)\n1183\t                                   'opaque '(elab-opaque local '[d])]\n1184\t                             '[(vector (is-opaque? (second (fetch-definition global 'd)))\n1185\t                                       (nbe-delta global [] '(d)))\n1186\t                               (vector (is-opaque? (second (fetch-definition opaque 'd)))\n1187\t                                       (nbe-delta opaque [] '(d)))\n1188\t                               (vector (is-opaque? (second (fetch-definition global 'd)))\n1189\t                                       (nbe-delta global [] '(d)))])))))\n1190\t  (testing \"duplicate transitions fail, and the context's original definition remains\"\n1191\t    (doseq [[flag step message] [[true :opaque \":opaque fails: definition is already opaque\"]\n1192\t                                 [false :transparent \":transparent fails: definition is not opaque\"]]]\n1193\t      (let [call (list 'elab-proof-step\n1194\t                       (list 'register-definition initial-context\n1195\t                             (list '->Definition ''d [] 0 ''body #{} ''T {:opaque flag}))\n1196\t                       [] [] {} step ''[d])\n1197\t            c (context-bc [] call)]\n1198\t        (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message message :yin.k/data {:name 'd}}] c)))))\n1199\t  (testing \"diagnostic proof arms preserve state and produce no hidden output\"\n1200\t    (doseq [step [:print-term :print-type :print-def :print-defenv]]\n1201\t      (is (= [:yin.k/ok [0 [{} {}]]]\n1202\t             (context-bc []\n1203\t                         (list 'let ['result (list 'elab-proof-step initial-context [] [] {} step [])\n1204\t                                     'k '(first (second result))]\n1205\t                               '[(:fresh k) (:definitions k)])))))))\n1206\t\n1207\t\n1208\t(def ^:private host-constant-unfold\n1209\t  ;; This admitted typed boundary is checked against the ACTUAL upstream\n1210\t  ;; typing/unfold-implicit, using only host-constant arguments (no inference).\n1211\t  '[(defn unfold-host-constants\n1212\t      [kernel ctx ddef args]\n1213\t      (unfold-typed-implicit kernel ctx ddef (mapv second args) (mapv second args)))])\n1214\t\n1215\t\n1216\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-shared-implicit-installation\n1217\t  (doseq [fn-form ['(fn [k ctx x] x)\n1218\t                   '(fn [k ctx x] (throw (ex-info \"extension failed\" {:msg \"data wins\" :extra 7})))]]\n1219\t    (let [implicit ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Implicit) 'i (eval fn-form))\n1220\t          args '([:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7])\n1221\t          a ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.typing/unfold-implicit) [{} {}] [] implicit args)\n1222\t          c (context-bc host-constant-unfold\n1223\t                        (list 'let ['k (list 'install-unfold-implicit initial-context 'unfold-host-constants)\n1224\t                                    'i (list '->Implicit ''i fn-form)]\n1225\t                              (list 'unfold-host-constants 'k [] 'i (list 'quote args))))]\n1226\t      (is (= [:yin.k/ok a] c) \"actual upstream catch and argument assembly, A/B/C\")))\n1227\t  (let [norm-binding (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/+unfold-implicit+)\n1228\t        nbe-binding (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.nbe/+unfold-implicit+)\n1229\t        args '([:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7])\n1230\t        implicit ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Implicit) 'i (fn [_ _ x] x))\n1231\t        env ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition) [{} {}] implicit)\n1232\t        a (with-redefs-fn {norm-binding (atom nil) nbe-binding (atom nil)}\n1233\t            (fn []\n1234\t              (let [f (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.typing/unfold-implicit)\n1235\t                    delta (fn []\n1236\t                            [((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.nbe/delta-reduction) env [] (cons 'i args))\n1237\t                             ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/delta-reduction) env [] (cons 'i args))])]\n1238\t                ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/install-unfold-implicit!) f)\n1239\t                (let [first-result (delta)]\n1240\t                  ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/install-unfold-implicit!) (fn [_ _ _ args] [:ok 'replacement args]))\n1241\t                  [first-result (delta) (identical? @@norm-binding @@nbe-binding)]))))\n1242\t        call (list 'let ['k0 (list 'register-definition initial-context '(->Implicit 'i (fn [k ctx x] x)))\n1243\t                         'k1 '(install-unfold-implicit k0 unfold-host-constants)\n1244\t                         'k2 '(install-unfold-implicit k1 (fn [k ctx ddef args] [:ok 'replacement args]))]\n1245\t                   '[(vector (nbe-delta k1 [] '(i [:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7]))\n1246\t                             (norm-delta k1 [] '(i [:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7])))\n1247\t                     (vector (nbe-delta k2 [] '(i [:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7]))\n1248\t                             (norm-delta k2 [] '(i [:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7])))\n1249\t                     true])]\n1250\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok a] (context-bc host-constant-unfold call))))\n1251\t  (testing \"extension installation is isolated and old bindings retain their value\"\n1252\t    (is (= [:yin.k/ok [true false true]]\n1253\t           (context-bc []\n1254\t                       (list 'let ['k0 initial-context\n1255\t                                   'k1 '(install-unfold-implicit k0 (fn [k ctx d args] [:ok 'installed args]))\n1256\t                                   'k2 '(install-opacity-function k1 missing-opacity-policy)]\n1257\t                             '[(= (:unfold-implicit k0) missing-unfold-implicit)\n1258\t                               (= (:unfold-implicit k1) (:unfold-implicit k0))\n1259\t                               (= (:opacity-policy k0) definition-opacity)]))))))\n1260\t\n1261\t\n1262\t(defn- assert-machine-data-within-budget!\n1263\t  \"Bound recursive validation work, which the VM instruction budget cannot\n1264\t   interrupt. Throw outside `is` so exhaustion also stops UCF reconstruction.\"\n1265\t  [value limit]\n1266\t  (let [visits (volatile! 0)\n1267\t        check vm/machine-data?\n1268\t        valid? (with-redefs [vm/machine-data?\n1269\t                             (fn [x]\n1270\t                               (when (> (vswap! visits inc) limit)\n1271\t                                 (throw (ex-info \"Machine-data validation budget exhausted\"\n1272\t                                                 {:visits @visits :limit limit})))\n1273\t                               (check x))]\n1274\t                 (vm/machine-data? value))]\n1275\t    (is valid?)\n1276\t    (is (<= @visits limit) \"descriptor environments have bounded validation work\")))\n1277\t\n1278\t\n1279\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-context-reconstruction\n1280\t  (let [program [(list 'let ['checkpoint\n1281\t                             (list 'let ['base initial-context 'offset 4]\n1282\t                                   '(register-unparser base :captured\n1283\t                                                       (fn [term] [(+ offset term) true])))]\n1284\t                       '(unparse checkpoint 3))]\n1285\t        forms (into (context-for program) program)\n1286\t        ast (yang/compile-program (into (yang/library-for forms) forms) true arg-vector-opts)\n1287\t        modules (oracle-registry yang/kind-module)\n1288\t        run-bounded (fn [machine]\n1289\t                      (loop [m machine n 0]\n1290\t                        (cond\n1291\t                          (vm/halted? m) (vm/value m)\n1292\t                          (= n 1000000)\n1293\t                          (throw (ex-info \"Context execution budget exhausted\" {:steps n}))\n1294\t                          :else (recur (vm/step m) (inc n)))))]\n1295\t    (is (vm/plain-data? context-source) \"adaptation is plain code data\")\n1296\t    (is (vm/plain-data? ast) \"runtime closures are never embedded as literals\")\n1297\t    (testing \"code rows round-trip and reconstruct the closure registry on both lanes\"\n1298\t      (let [[_root datoms] (vm/ast->datoms-with-root ast)\n1299\t            rebuilt (vm/datoms->ast (cbor/decode (cbor/encode datoms)))]\n1300\t        (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\n1301\t          (is (= [:yin.k/ok 7] (compiler-test/run-guest-ast rebuilt modules lane 1000000))))))\n1302\t    (testing \"a live registry with a captured guest closure survives UCF reconstruction\"\n1303\t      (let [code (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n1304\t            bytecode (:vector (linearize/project-rows code))\n1305\t            source-index {(ucf/code-address bytecode) #{(:root code)}}\n1306\t            machine (semantic/load-vector (rows-support/new-machine {:modules modules})\n1307\t                                          bytecode vm/semantic-contract)\n1308\t            checkpoint (loop [m machine n 0]\n1309\t                         (cond\n1310\t                           (get-in m [:env 'checkpoint]) m\n1311\t                           (or (vm/halted? m) (= n 1000000))\n1312\t                           (throw (ex-info \"Context checkpoint was not reached\" {:steps n}))\n1313\t                           :else (recur (vm/step m) (inc n))))\n1314\t            k (get-in checkpoint [:env 'checkpoint])\n1315\t            _ (is (values/closure? (get-in k [:unparser-registry :unparsers :captured\n1316\t                                              :yang.call/entry])))\n1317\t            _ (assert-machine-data-within-budget! k 100000)\n1318\t            wire (rows/lift-task checkpoint (rows-support/serve-table) {:source-index source-index})\n1319\t            _ (is (vm/plain-data? wire) \"serialized context contains code references, not host closures\")\n1320\t            {:keys [attach!]} (rows-support/attacher)\n1321\t            restored (rows/lower-task (rows-support/new-machine {:modules modules})\n1322\t                                      (cbor/decode (cbor/encode wire)) attach!)\n1323\t            k' (get-in restored [:env 'checkpoint])]\n1324\t        (is (values/closure? (get-in k' [:unparser-registry :unparsers :captured\n1325\t                                         :yang.call/entry])))\n1326\t        (assert-machine-data-within-budget! k' 100000)\n1327\t        (is (= [:yin.k/ok 7] (run-bounded restored)))\n1328\t        (is (= [:yin.k/ok 7] (run-bounded checkpoint))))))\n1329\t  (testing \"host callbacks cannot enter code data through registry literals\"\n1330\t    (is (thrown? Exception\n1331\t          (encoder/project\n1332\t            (encoder/source-envelope\n1333\t              :program \"slice8-host-callback-refusal\"\n1334\t              [{:type :literal :value {:unparser-registry {:unparsers {:bad identity}}}}]))))))\n1335\t\n1336\t\n1337\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-admission\n1338\t  (let [symbols (set (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq context-forms)))\n1339\t        ambient '#{atom swap! reset! deref clojure.core/deref resolve var? alter-var-root\n1340\t                   defrecord println print pprint pp/pprint nano-time System/nanoTime}]\n1341\t    (is (empty? (filter symbols ambient)) \"context source has no ambient state, host lookup or diagnostics\")\n1342\t    (is (vm/plain-data? context-forms)))\n1343\t  (testing \"free-symbol admission catches undeclared guest dependencies before execution\"\n1344\t    (is (= '#{missing-extension}\n1345\t           (unbound-ast-symbols (yang/compile '(fn [x] (missing-extension x))) []))))\n1346\t  (testing \"context modules reject undeclared namespace lookup at admission\"\n1347\t    (doseq [call ['(resolve 'clojure.core/map)]]\n1348\t      (is (thrown-with-msg? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo #\"Unadmitted context dependencies\"\n1349\t            (run-outcome [] call (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) true))))))\n1350\t\n1351\t\n1352\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-implicit-delta-errors\n1353\t  (let [fail-form '(fn [kernel ctx x]\n1354\t                     (throw (ex-info \"extension failed\" {:msg \"data wins\" :extra 7})))\n1355\t        implicit ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Implicit) 'i (eval fail-form))\n1356\t        env ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition) [{} {}] implicit)\n1357\t        term '(i [:latte-kernel.presyntax/host-constant 7])]\n1358\t    (doseq [[a-name c-name] [['latte-kernel.nbe/delta-reduction 'nbe-delta]\n1359\t                             ['latte-kernel.norm/delta-reduction 'norm-delta]]]\n1360\t      (let [a (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/+unfold-implicit+) (atom nil)\n1361\t                               (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.nbe/+unfold-implicit+) (atom nil)}\n1362\t                (fn []\n1363\t                  ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/install-unfold-implicit!)\n1364\t                   (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.typing/unfold-implicit))\n1365\t                  (a-leg (upstream-fn a-name) [env [] term])))\n1366\t            c (context-bc host-constant-unfold\n1367\t                          (list 'let ['k (list 'register-definition\n1368\t                                               (list 'install-unfold-implicit initial-context 'unfold-host-constants)\n1369\t                                               (list '->Implicit ''i fail-form))]\n1370\t                                (list c-name 'k [] (list 'quote term))))]\n1371\t        (is (agrees? a c))))))\n1372\t\n1373\t\n1374\t(defn- a-opacity-proof\n1375\t  ([script] (a-opacity-proof script false))\n1376\t  ([script install?]\n1377\t   (let [ns-sym (gensym \"latte-proof-a-\")\n1378\t         sandbox (create-ns ns-sym)\n1379\t         ddef ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition) 'd [] 0 'body #{} 'T {})\n1380\t         policy (fn [v flag] (alter-var-root v assoc-in [:opts :opaque] flag))]\n1381\t     (try\n1382\t       (intern sandbox 'd ddef)\n1383\t       (binding [*ns* sandbox]\n1384\t         (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.proof/+opacity-fn+)\n1385\t                          (atom (if install?\n1386\t                                  (fn [_ _] (throw (ex-info \"Policy not installed\" {}))) policy))}\n1387\t           (fn []\n1388\t             (when install?\n1389\t               ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.proof/install-opacity-function) policy))\n1390\t             (a-leg (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof) [[{} {}] [] script]))))\n1391\t       (finally (remove-ns ns-sym))))))\n1392\t\n1393\t\n1394\t(deftest test-oracle-slice8-upstream-proof-loop\n1395\t  (testing \"the original proof loop threads updated contexts across state steps\"\n1396\t    (doseq [script ['((:opaque d) (:transparent d) (:opaque d) (:transparent d))\n1397\t                    '((:opaque d) (:opaque d))\n1398\t                    '((:opaque d) (:transparent d) (:transparent d))]]\n1399\t      (let [a (a-opacity-proof script)\n1400\t            c (context-bc []\n1401\t                          (list 'elab-proof\n1402\t                                (list 'register-definition initial-context '(->Definition 'd [] 0 'body #{} 'T {}))\n1403\t                                [] (list 'quote script)))]\n1404\t        (is (agrees? a c) \"A uses updated Vars; B/C use the returned definition environment\")))))\n1405\t\n1406\t\n1407\t;; =============================================================================\n1408\t;; Slice 9: a fail-closed kernel gate. Historical slice tests are not the gate.\n1409\t;; =============================================================================\n1410\t\n1411\t(def ^:private kernel-gate-corpus\n1412\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn\"))))\n1413\t\n1414\t\n1415\t(def ^:private kernel-fixture-closure\n1416\t  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/fixture_closure.edn\"))))\n1417\t\n1418\t\n1419\t(defn- kernel-symbol\n1420\t  [{:keys [ns name]}]\n1421\t  (symbol (str/replace (str ns) \"_\" \"-\") (str name)))\n1422\t\n1423\t\n1424\t(defn- kernel-guest-name\n1425\t  [s]\n1426\t  (symbol (str \"gate-\" (last (str/split (namespace s) #\"\\.\")) \"-\" (name s))))\n1427\t\n1428\t\n1429\t(defn- kernel-arities\n1430\t  [form]\n1431\t  (when (#{'defn 'defn-} (first form))\n1432\t    (let [header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) (nnext form))\n1433\t          params (if (vector? (first header)) [(first header)] (map first header))]\n1434\t      (mapv (fn [p] (if (some #{'&} p) [:variadic (.indexOf p '&)] (count p))) params))))\n1435\t\n1436\t\n1437\t(def ^:private kernel-entries\n1438\t  (mapv (fn [entry]\n1439\t          (let [s (kernel-symbol entry)]\n1440\t            (upstream-fn s) ; load the real aliases and refers before resolving source\n1441\t            (assoc entry :symbol s :arities (kernel-arities (get top-forms [(:ns entry) (:name entry)])))))\n1442\t        manifest))\n1443\t\n1444\t\n1445\t(defn- kernel-resolve\n1446\t  [ns-sym s]\n1447\t  (when (symbol? s)\n1448\t    (let [n (the-ns (symbol (str/replace (str ns-sym) \"_\" \"-\")))\n1449\t          v (ns-resolve n s)]\n1450\t      (when (and (var? v) (str/starts-with? (str (:ns (meta v))) \"latte-kernel.\"))\n1451\t        (symbol (str (:ns (meta v))) (str (:name (meta v))))))))\n1452\t\n1453\t\n1454\t(defn- kernel-rewrite\n1455\t  \"Resolve library names against their actual upstream namespace, respecting\n1456\t   lexical binders and quote. No blanket alias stripping or data rewriting.\"\n1457\t  [ns-sym form]\n1458\t  (letfn [(bindings [pattern] (set (filter symbol? (tree-seq coll? seq pattern))))\n1459\t          (forms [xs bound] (map #(step % bound) xs))\n1460\t          (arity\n1461\t            [xs bound]\n1462\t            (let [[params & body] xs\n1463\t                  body (forms body (into bound (bindings params)))\n1464\t                  body (if (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.syntax) (= 'free-vars (second form))\n1465\t                                (= '[def-env t] params))\n1466\t                         [(list* 'let '[def-env (if (map? def-env) (:definitions def-env) def-env)] body)]\n1467\t                         body)]\n1468\t              (list* params body)))\n1469\t          (step\n1470\t            [x bound]\n1471\t            (cond\n1472\t              (symbol? x) (cond\n1473\t                            (contains? bound x) x\n1474\t                            (#{\"set\" \"clojure.set\"} (namespace x)) (symbol (name x))\n1475\t                            (= \"pp\" (namespace x)) (symbol \"clojure.pprint\" (name x))\n1476\t                            (contains? '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\n1477\t                                         ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\n1478\t                            (get '{get-in lookup-in not-empty context-not-empty\n1479\t                                   ffirst context-ffirst list* context-list-star} x)\n1480\t                            :else (if-let [s (kernel-resolve ns-sym x)]\n1481\t                                    ;; empty-env at the immutable-context boundary\n1482\t                                    ;; is the same explicit initialization used by\n1483\t                                    ;; the slice-8 fixtures, including default arities.\n1484\t                                    (if (= s 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\n1485\t                                      initial-context\n1486\t                                      (if (and (= \"latte-kernel.defenv\" (namespace s))\n1487\t                                               (str/starts-with? (name s) \"->\"))\n1488\t                                        (symbol (name s)) (kernel-guest-name s))) x))\n1489\t              (seq? x)\n1490\t              (let [[op & xs] x]\n1491\t                (cond\n1492\t                  (= op 'quote) x\n1493\t                  (and (= op 'lazy-seq) (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.utils) (= 'zip (second form)))\n1494\t                  (step (second x) bound)\n1495\t                  (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.proof) (= 'elab-proof-step (second form))\n1496\t                       (#{'(do (elab-opaque def-env args) [:cont [def-env ctx var-deps def-uses]])\n1497\t                          '(do (elab-transparent def-env args) [:cont [def-env ctx var-deps def-uses]])} x))\n1498\t                  (list 'let ['next-env (step (second x) bound)]\n1499\t                        '[:cont [next-env ctx var-deps def-uses]])\n1500\t                  (#{'fn 'fn*} op)\n1501\t                  (cons 'fn (if (vector? (first xs)) (arity xs bound)\n1502\t                                (map #(arity % bound) xs)))\n1503\t                  (#{'let 'loop} op)\n1504\t                  (let [[bs & body] xs\n1505\t                        [bs' scope] (reduce (fn [[out scope] [p init]]\n1506\t                                              (let [have-type? (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.proof)\n1507\t                                                                    (= 'elab-have-impl (second form))\n1508\t                                                                    (= p '[status rec-ty]))\n1509\t                                                    ;; Both type branches return their context to the\n1510\t                                                    ;; enclosing have step, including anonymous have.\n1511\t                                                    init (if have-type?\n1512\t                                                           (let [[_ test inferred [_ bs result]] init]\n1513\t                                                             (list 'if test [inferred 'def-env]\n1514\t                                                                   (list 'let bs [result 'def-env]))) init)\n1515\t                                                    p (cond\n1516\t                                                        have-type? [p 'def-env]\n1517\t                                                        (and (seq? init)\n1518\t                                                             (= 'latte-kernel.typing/rebuild-type\n1519\t                                                                (kernel-resolve ns-sym (first init))))\n1520\t                                                        ;; check-proof calls this with def-env', so\n1521\t                                                        ;; retain the caller's actual context binding.\n1522\t                                                        [p (second init)]\n1523\t                                                        :else p)]\n1524\t                                                [(conj out p (step init scope)) (into scope (bindings p))]))\n1525\t                                            [[] bound] (partition 2 bs))]\n1526\t                    (list* op bs' (forms body scope)))\n1527\t                  ;; The slice-8 delta boundary: both namespaces use one binding.\n1528\t                  (and (#{'deref 'clojure.core/deref} op) (= xs '(+unfold-implicit+)))\n1529\t                  '(:unfold-implicit def-env)\n1530\t                  :else (apply list (forms x bound))))\n1531\t              (vector? x) (mapv #(step % bound) x)\n1532\t              (map? x) (into (empty x) (map (fn [[k v]] [(step k bound) (step v bound)])) x)\n1533\t              (set? x) (into #{} (forms x bound))\n1534\t              :else x))]\n1535\t    (let [[kind fname & header] form\n1536\t          header (drop-while #(not (or (vector? %) (seq? %))) header)\n1537\t          guest (kernel-guest-name (kernel-symbol {:ns ns-sym :name fname}))]\n1538\t      (if (#{'defn 'defn-} kind)\n1539\t        (list* 'defn guest\n1540\t               (if (vector? (first header)) (arity header #{}) (map #(arity % #{}) header)))\n1541\t        (list 'def guest (step (nth form 2) #{}))))))\n1542\t\n1543\t\n1544\t(def ^:private kernel-context-adapters\n1545\t  ;; Reuse the established slice-8 representation boundary; no new compiler\n1546\t  ;; workaround or truncated proof-step dispatcher is admitted here.\n1547\t  '#{definition? theorem? axiom? notation? implicit? latte-definition?\n1548\t     local-definitions register-definition fetch-definition registered-definition? qualify-def})\n1549\t\n1550\t\n1551\t(defn- kernel-source\n1552\t  [{:keys [ns name symbol arities disposition admission-reason]}]\n1553\t  (cond\n1554\t    (= :excluded disposition)\n1555\t    (list* 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol)\n1556\t           (map (fn [n]\n1557\t                  (list (mapv #(clojure.core/symbol (str \"p\" %)) (range n))\n1558\t                        (list 'throw (list 'ex-info \"Excluded nonportable kernel binding\"\n1559\t                                           {:refusal :nonportable-binding :binding (list 'quote symbol) :reason admission-reason})))) arities))\n1560\t    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.defenv) (contains? kernel-context-adapters name))\n1561\t    (list* 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol)\n1562\t           (map (fn [n]\n1563\t                  (let [ps (mapv #(clojure.core/symbol (str \"p\" %)) (range n))]\n1564\t                    (list ps (list* name ps)))) arities))\n1565\t    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.proof) (= name '+opacity-fn+))\n1566\t    ;; The old ambient binding now names the explicit field; evaluating this\n1567\t    ;; binding cannot initialize an atom or install an implicit closure.\n1568\t    (list 'def (kernel-guest-name symbol) :opacity-policy)\n1569\t    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.typing) (= name 'rebuild-type))\n1570\t    ;; This allocation boundary returns the updated context explicitly. Its\n1571\t    ;; original [status type] result remains the first component.\n1572\t    (list 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol) '[def-env ctx ty]\n1573\t          '(let [[vfresh supply] (fresh-symbol {:counter (:fresh def-env)} \"fresh\")\n1574\t                 [status ty' _] (gate-typing-type-of-term def-env (cons [vfresh ty] ctx) vfresh)]\n1575\t             [[status ty'] (assoc def-env :fresh (:counter supply))]))\n1576\t    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.proof)\n1577\t         (contains? '#{elab-opaque elab-transparent install-opacity-function is-opaque?} name))\n1578\t    (let [adapter (first (filter #(= name (second %)) context-forms))]\n1579\t      (list* 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol) (drop 2 adapter)))\n1580\t    :else (kernel-rewrite ns (get top-forms [ns name]))))\n1581\t\n1582\t\n1583\t(def ^:private kernel-declaration-refusals\n1584\t  ;; Pinned upstream declares this function but never defines it. Keeping a\n1585\t  ;; loud branch-local refusal lets unrelated typing paths compile; executing\n1586\t  ;; that branch is still a blocked fixture, never an accepted rejection.\n1587\t  '[(defn gate-typing-type-of-ascribe\n1588\t      [def-env ctx e u]\n1589\t      (throw (ex-info \"Pinned upstream declaration has no definition\"\n1590\t                      {:refusal :upstream-unbound\n1591\t                       :binding 'latte-kernel.typing/type-of-ascribe})))])\n1592\t\n1593\t\n1594\t(def ^:private kernel-sources\n1595\t  (into (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) kernel-declaration-refusals)\n1596\t        (map (fn [entry] [(kernel-guest-name (:symbol entry)) (kernel-source entry)])) kernel-entries))\n1597\t\n1598\t\n1599\t(defn- kernel-call\n1600\t  [form]\n1601\t  ;; Fixture code uses fully qualified names. Constructor adapters are the\n1602\t  ;; five existing context constructors, outside the 143-binding manifest.\n1603\t  (letfn [(rewrite\n1604\t            [x]\n1605\t            (cond\n1606\t              (and (seq? x) (= 'quote (first x))) x\n1607\t              (symbol? x) (if (and (namespace x) (str/starts-with? (namespace x) \"latte-kernel.\"))\n1608\t                            (if (str/starts-with? (name x) \"->\") (symbol (name x)) (kernel-guest-name x)) x)\n1609\t              (seq? x) (apply list (map rewrite x))\n1610\t              (vector? x) (mapv rewrite x)\n1611\t              (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(rewrite k) (rewrite v)])) x)\n1612\t              (set? x) (set (map rewrite x))\n1613\t              :else x))]\n1614\t    (rewrite form)))\n1615\t\n1616\t\n1617\t(defn- kernel-closure\n1618\t  [call]\n1619\t  (let [sources (merge (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) context-forms) kernel-sources)\n1620\t        mentions #(filter (set (keys sources)) (walk-symbols %))\n1621\t        needed (loop [todo (seq (mentions call)) seen #{}]\n1622\t                 (if-let [n (first todo)]\n1623\t                   (if (contains? seen n) (recur (next todo) seen)\n1624\t                       (recur (concat (next todo) (mentions (get sources n))) (conj seen n))) seen))\n1625\t        ordered (concat context-forms kernel-declaration-refusals (map #(get kernel-sources (kernel-guest-name (:symbol %))) kernel-entries))]\n1626\t    (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) ordered)))\n1627\t\n1628\t\n1629\t(defn- kernel-fixture-call\n1630\t  [{:keys [call guest-call definitions project-proof?]} guest?]\n1631\t  (let [env (if guest? initial-context 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\n1632\t        register (if guest? 'register-definition 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition)\n1633\t        env (reduce (fn [env definition] (list register env (if guest? (kernel-call definition) definition))) env definitions)\n1634\t        call (if guest? (kernel-call (or guest-call call)) call)\n1635\t        call (if project-proof?\n1636\t               (list 'let ['r call] '(if (= :ok (first r)) [:ok (rest (second r))] r)) call)]\n1637\t    (list 'let ['env env] call)))\n1638\t\n1639\t\n1640\t(defn- evidence-data\n1641\t  \"EDN evidence retains all portable values and metadata. Nonportable host\n1642\t   payloads are explicit evidence, not accepted representation differences.\"\n1643\t  [x]\n1644\t  (cond\n1645\t    (fn? x) {:nonportable-host-value (str (class x))}\n1646\t    (record? x) (evidence-data (upstream-record-data x))\n1647\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(evidence-data k) (evidence-data v)])) x)\n1648\t    (vector? x) (mapv evidence-data x)\n1649\t    (set? x) (set (map evidence-data x))\n1650\t    (seq? x) (apply list (map evidence-data x))\n1651\t    :else x))\n1652\t\n1653\t\n1654\t(defn- kernel-attempt\n1655\t  [f]\n1656\t  (try (f)\n1657\t       (catch Exception e\n1658\t         {:status :blocked :message (ex-message e)\n1659\t          ;; Observer exceptions attach the entire host VM as :session. It is\n1660\t          ;; diagnostic machinery, not a portable domain payload; recursively\n1661\t          ;; expanding its closure environments duplicates the whole program.\n1662\t          :data (evidence-data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session))\n1663\t          :host-session-attached? (contains? (ex-data e) :session)\n1664\t          :causes (mapv (fn [cause] {:class (str (class cause)) :message (ex-message cause)})\n1665\t                        (take-while some? (iterate ex-cause e)))\n1666\t          :exception (str (class e))})))\n1667\t\n1668\t\n1669\t(defn- kernel-a\n1670\t  [fixture]\n1671\t  (kernel-attempt\n1672\t    #(let [value (cond\n1673\t                   (#{:opacity-proof :opacity-install} (:mode fixture))\n1674\t                   (let [outcome (a-opacity-proof (:script fixture) (= :opacity-install (:mode fixture)))]\n1675\t                     (if (= :ok (first (:value outcome)))\n1676\t                       (update outcome :value (fn [v] [:ok (rest (second v))])) outcome))\n1677\t                   (= :unfold-install (:mode fixture))\n1678\t                   (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.norm/+unfold-implicit+) (atom nil)\n1679\t                                    (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.nbe/+unfold-implicit+) (atom nil)}\n1680\t                     (fn [] (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) [])))\n1681\t                   (= :namespace-isolation (:mode fixture))\n1682\t                   (let [sandbox (create-ns (gensym \"gate-ambient-a-\"))]\n1683\t                     (try\n1684\t                       (intern sandbox 'gate-ambient-definition\n1685\t                               ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.defenv/->Definition)\n1686\t                                'gate-ambient-definition [] 0 'ambient #{} 'T {}))\n1687\t                       (binding [*ns* sandbox]\n1688\t                         (refer 'clojure.core)\n1689\t                         (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) []))\n1690\t                       (finally (remove-ns (ns-name sandbox)))))\n1691\t                   (#{:unparser :unparser-install} (:mode fixture))\n1692\t                   (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/+unparser-registry+)\n1693\t                                    (atom {:fundamental [] :standard [] :user [] :unparsers {}})}\n1694\t                     (fn []\n1695\t                       (if (= :unparser-install (:mode fixture))\n1696\t                         (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) [])\n1697\t                         (do\n1698\t                           ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser!) :gate (eval (:extension fixture)))\n1699\t                           (a-leg (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse) [(:term fixture)])))))\n1700\t                   :else (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) []))]\n1701\t       {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data value) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data value))})))\n1702\t\n1703\t\n1704\t(defn- kernel-c-program\n1705\t  [fixture]\n1706\t  (if (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\n1707\t    (list 'unparse (list 'register-unparser initial-context :gate (:extension fixture)) (list 'quote (:term fixture)))\n1708\t    (kernel-fixture-call fixture true)))\n1709\t\n1710\t\n1711\t(defn- kernel-b\n1712\t  [fixture]\n1713\t  (kernel-attempt\n1714\t    #(let [sandbox (create-ns (gensym \"kernel-gate-b-\"))\n1715\t           call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n1716\t           forms (kernel-closure call)\n1717\t           host-form (fn [form]\n1718\t                       ;; Preserve the actual one-argument gensym call. Only\n1719\t                       ;; the slice-8 explicit two-argument supply is adapted.\n1720\t                       (walk/postwalk\n1721\t                         (fn [x]\n1722\t                           (if (and (seq? x) (= 'gensym (first x)) (= 2 (count x)))\n1723\t                             (cons 'clojure.core/gensym (rest x)) x)) form))]\n1724\t       (try\n1725\t         (binding [*ns* sandbox]\n1726\t           (refer 'clojure.core)\n1727\t           (require '[clojure.set :refer [union difference]])\n1728\t           (eval (list* 'declare\n1729\t                        (concat (map second forms)\n1730\t                                (for [[ns-sym source] all-forms\n1731\t                                      form source :when (= 'declare (first form))\n1732\t                                      s (rest form)\n1733\t                                      :let [qualified (kernel-resolve ns-sym s)]\n1734\t                                      :when qualified]\n1735\t                                  (kernel-guest-name qualified)))))\n1736\t           (doseq [form forms] (eval (context-host-form (host-form form))))\n1737\t           (let [v (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (context-host-form (host-form call)))) [])]\n1738\t             {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\n1739\t         (finally (remove-ns (ns-name sandbox)))))))\n1740\t\n1741\t\n1742\t(def ^:private kernel-context-integration-names\n1743\t  ;; Integrations also enter existing explicit-context adapters directly,\n1744\t  ;; rather than their gate-* wrappers. Keep those identities explicit.\n1745\t  {'latte-kernel.defenv/local-definitions 'local-definitions\n1746\t   'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition 'register-definition\n1747\t   'latte-kernel.proof/is-opaque? 'is-opaque?\n1748\t   'latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! 'unregister-unparser\n1749\t   'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse 'unparse\n1750\t   'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser! 'register-unparser\n1751\t   'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse-term-once 'unparse-term-once\n1752\t   'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse-term-rec