{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_VSvF1ssLm4AwZBeu0Z9PhKb5","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.values\n2\t  \"The in-machine closure and continuation values (D7).\n3\t\n4\t   A closure and a captured continuation are host types minted only by a\n5\t   kernel, never by a guest primitive or a module export. `closure?` and\n6\t   `continuation?` are type tests, so an ordinary map is always data,\n7\t   including one carrying `:type :closure` or `:type :reified-continuation`:\n8\t   a program cannot forge either by building its map.\n9\t\n10\t   Each type wraps the kernel's own payload map unchanged, plus an owner\n11\t   tag: the task the value was minted in (`owner-tag`). Lift, lower,\n12\t   completion and heap reclamation read the payload, so they keep operating\n13\t   on the maps they already understand.\n14\t\n15\t   Neither type answers keyword lookup, unlike `yin.vm.effect`'s `Effect`:\n16\t   a guest `get` on a closure answers nil, never its captured environment.\n17\t   Neither is a function: `fn?` is false, so no kernel's primitive arm is\n18\t   taken. Equality is structural over kind, owner and payload, and hash\n19\t   agrees with it, so two runs of one program give equal VM states and a\n20\t   closure can be a set member or a map key.\n21\t\n22\t   Both print opaquely, on every host and through `str`, `pr-str` and every\n23\t   guest print: `{:type :closure}` or `{:type :continuation}`, never the\n24\t   payload, a captured value, or the owner tag (`marker-text`).\n25\t\n26\t   These are table C laws of docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md\n27\t   (§4.2), which a port must meet: equal iff kind, owner and payload are\n28\t   equal; hash of `[kind owner payload]`; print the marker text.\n29\t\n30\t   Cell, stream and cursor references stay sealed plain data: they name\n31\t   table entries, are already unforgeable, and must stay usable as keys.\"\n32\t  (:require [dao.host.integer :as integer-host]\n33\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n34\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n35\t\n36\t\n37\t(def marker-text\n38\t  \"The opaque printed form of each kind, shaped like the REPL's\n39\t   `{:type :host-fn}` marker.\"\n40\t  {:closure \"{:type :closure}\", :continuation \"{:type :continuation}\"})\n41\t\n42\t\n43\t(deftype Closure\n44\t  [owner payload]\n45\t  #?@(:cljd [cljd.core/IEquiv\n46\t             (-equiv [_ other]\n47\t                     (and (instance? Closure other)\n48\t                          (= owner (.-owner ^Closure other))\n49\t                          (= payload (.-payload ^Closure other))))\n50\t             cljd.core/IHash\n51\t             (-hash [_] (hash [:closure owner payload]))\n52\t             cljd.core/IPrint\n53\t             (-print [_ sink] (.write sink (:closure marker-text)))\n54\t             Object\n55\t             (toString [_] (:closure marker-text))]\n56\t      :clj [Object\n57\t            (equals [_ other]\n58\t                    (and (instance? Closure other)\n59\t                         (= owner (.-owner ^Closure other))\n60\t                         (= payload (.-payload ^Closure other))))\n61\t            (hashCode [_] (hash [:closure owner payload]))\n62\t            (toString [_] (:closure marker-text))\n63\t            clojure.lang.IHashEq\n64\t            (hasheq [_] (hash [:closure owner payload]))]\n65\t      :cljs [IEquiv\n66\t             (-equiv [_ other]\n67\t                     (and (instance? Closure other)\n68\t                          (= owner (.-owner ^Closure other))\n69\t                          (= payload (.-payload ^Closure other))))\n70\t             IHash\n71\t             (-hash [_] (hash [:closure owner payload]))\n72\t             IPrintWithWriter\n73\t             (-pr-writer [_ writer _opts]\n74\t                         (-write writer (:closure marker-text)))\n75\t             Object\n76\t             (toString [_] (:closure marker-text))]))\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t(deftype Continuation\n80\t  [owner payload]\n81\t  #?@(:cljd [cljd.core/IEquiv\n82\t             (-equiv [_ other]\n83\t                     (and (instance? Continuation other)\n84\t                          (= owner (.-owner ^Continuation other))\n85\t                          (= payload (.-payload ^Continuation other))))\n86\t             cljd.core/IHash\n87\t             (-hash [_] (hash [:continuation owner payload]))\n88\t             cljd.core/IPrint\n89\t             (-print [_ sink] (.write sink (:continuation marker-text)))\n90\t             Object\n91\t             (toString [_] (:continuation marker-text))]\n92\t      :clj [Object\n93\t            (equals [_ other]\n94\t                    (and (instance? Continuation other)\n95\t                         (= owner (.-owner ^Continuation other))\n96\t                         (= payload (.-payload ^Continuation other))))\n97\t            (hashCode [_] (hash [:continuation owner payload]))\n98\t            (toString [_] (:continuation marker-text))\n99\t            clojure.lang.IHashEq\n100\t            (hasheq [_] (hash [:continuation owner payload]))]\n101\t      :cljs [IEquiv\n102\t             (-equiv [_ other]\n103\t                     (and (instance? Continuation other)\n104\t                          (= owner (.-owner ^Continuation other))\n105\t                          (= payload (.-payload ^Continuation other))))\n106\t             IHash\n107\t             (-hash [_] (hash [:continuation owner payload]))\n108\t             IPrintWithWriter\n109\t             (-pr-writer [_ writer _opts]\n110\t                         (-write writer (:continuation marker-text)))\n111\t             Object\n112\t             (toString [_] (:continuation marker-text))]))\n113\t\n114\t\n115\t#?(:cljd nil\n116\t   :clj (defmethod print-method Closure\n117\t          [_ ^java.io.Writer w]\n118\t          (.write w ^String (:closure marker-text))))\n119\t\n120\t\n121\t#?(:cljd nil\n122\t   :clj (defmethod print-method Continuation\n123\t          [_ ^java.io.Writer w]\n124\t          (.write w ^String (:continuation marker-text))))\n125\t\n126\t\n127\t(defn owner-tag\n128\t  \"The owner tag of the task whose capability secret is `secret`: derived\n129\t   once, held in VM state, and carried by every closure and continuation\n130\t   the task mints. It reveals nothing of the secret. A task without a\n131\t   secret has owner nil.\"\n132\t  [secret]\n133\t  (when (some? secret)\n134\t    (jing/content-hash [:yin.k/owner secret] {:algorithm :blake3})))\n135\t\n136\t\n137\t(defn closure\n138\t  \"Mint a closure owned by `owner` over the kernel payload map `payload`.\n139\t   A trusted constructor: only kernels call it, never a guest primitive.\"\n140\t  [owner payload]\n141\t  (Closure. owner payload))\n142\t\n143\t\n144\t(defn continuation\n145\t  \"Mint a captured continuation owned by `owner` over the kernel payload\n146\t   map `payload`. A trusted constructor, as `closure`.\"\n147\t  [owner payload]\n148\t  (Continuation. owner payload))\n149\t\n150\t\n151\t(defn closure?\n152\t  \"True when `x` is a closure a kernel minted. A type test: no map is a\n153\t   closure, whatever keys it carries.\"\n154\t  [x]\n155\t  (instance? Closure x))\n156\t\n157\t\n158\t(defn continuation?\n159\t  \"True when `x` is a continuation a kernel captured. A type test.\"\n160\t  [x]\n161\t  (instance? Continuation x))\n162\t\n163\t\n164\t(defn host-typed?\n165\t  \"True when `x` is a closure or a continuation.\"\n166\t  [x]\n167\t  (or (closure? x) (continuation? x)))\n168\t\n169\t\n170\t(defn payload\n171\t  \"The kernel payload map of closure or continuation `x`.\"\n172\t  [x]\n173\t  (if (closure? x)\n174\t    (.-payload ^Closure x)\n175\t    (.-payload ^Continuation x)))\n176\t\n177\t\n178\t(defn owner\n179\t  \"The owner tag of closure or continuation `x`.\"\n180\t  [x]\n181\t  (if (closure? x)\n182\t    (.-owner ^Closure x)\n183\t    (.-owner ^Continuation x)))\n184\t\n185\t\n186\t(defn owned-by?\n187\t  \"True when closure or continuation `x` was minted by the task whose\n188\t   owner tag is `tag`.\"\n189\t  [x tag]\n190\t  (let [o (owner x)]\n191\t    (or (identical? o tag) (= o tag))))\n192\t\n193\t\n194\t(defn kind-of\n195\t  \"The coarse kind of `x` a refusal may carry in place of the value\n196\t   itself: never the value, so a refusal leaks nothing it was handed.\"\n197\t  [x]\n198\t  (cond (nil? x) :nil\n199\t        (boolean? x) :boolean\n200\t        (or (number? x) (integer-host/big-carrier? x) (cbor/float64? x))\n201\t        :number\n202\t        (string? x) :string\n203\t        (keyword? x) :keyword\n204\t        (symbol? x) :symbol\n205\t        (closure? x) :closure\n206\t        (continuation? x) :continuation\n207\t        (fn? x) :host-fn\n208\t        (map? x) :map\n209\t        (vector? x) :vector\n210\t        (set? x) :set\n211\t        (seq? x) :seq\n212\t        :else :host-object))"}
