       (if (= node u/capture) (u/lit :invalid-continuation) node))\n1357\t              (outcome-ast '[(defn f\n1358\t                               []\n1359\t                               1) (+ 1 (f))]))]\n1360\t    (doseq [run [walker-run semantic-run]]\n1361\t      (let [result (first (run ast))]\n1362\t        (is (= :yin.k/error (first result)))\n1363\t        (is (= {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n1364\t                :yang.call/data {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}}\n1365\t               (second result)))))))\n1366\t\n1367\t\n1368\t(deftest test-common-call-rejects-named-arguments\n1369\t  (let [forms '[(defn f\n1370\t                  [x]\n1371\t                  x)\n1372\t                (let [condition (yang.call/invoke f [] [[\"x\" 1]] profile-raise)\n1373\t                      value (get condition :yang.call/value)]\n1374\t                  [(get condition :yang.call/reason)"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_V9tZNT3aZ8a1rV5uOBKO2mNo","content":"3514\t### 8.10 Shared function calling convention\n3515\t\n3516\t**Status: proposed, 2026-10-29; not implemented.** This section specifies\n3517\tone invocation convention for every conforming ANTLR-based Yang frontend.\n3518\tExamples are non-exhaustive. Adding a language must not add a case to Yang\n3519\tcore, a language-pair bridge, or an evaluator transition. The words\n3520\t**must**, **must not**, and **may** state requirements on a future\n3521\tconforming implementation, not claims about current code.\n3522\t\n3523\t#### 8.10.1 Decision and scope\n3524\t\n3525\tA Yin function is a Yin function, independent of its source syntax. The\n3526\tVM applies a closure to operands. Source calling semantics are ordinary\n3527\tUAST implementing the call site and callee entry, above the VM.\n3528\t\n3529\tEvery supported source-level callable, after its source-required\n3530\tresolution, exposes `:yang.call/entry`, an ordinary Yin closure taking\n3531\texactly one invocation record. Invoking it is an ordinary\n3532\t`:application`. No AST tag, lambda slot, instruction, host primitive,\n3533\teffect kind, or source-language test is added to the VM.\n3534\t\n3535\tThis is an internal calling convention, not a transport, another system\n3536\tABI, or a host callback interface. Calls between source languages inside\n3537\tone task do not themselves cross a host boundary. Portable I/O and\n3538\tcross-task interaction continue through `dao.stream`.\n3539\t\n3540\t**Transparent calling** means that an admitted callable can be passed,\n3541\tstored, returned, and invoked by any conforming frontend without a\n3542\thandwritten language-pair wrapper. It does not mean every foreign value\n3543\tsatisfies every source operation. Invocation, name visibility, and value\n3544\tinterpretation are distinct obligations.\n3545\t\n3546\tThe convention covers ordinary source calls and supported callable\n3547\tobjects, including higher-order calls. It does not make macros runtime\n3548\tfunctions, grant JavaScript `[[Construct]]`, turn a generator into an\n3549\tordinary returning function, or add a source feature a frontend refuses.\n3550\tConstructors and asynchronous operations keep their declared source\n3551\tsemantics; ordinary callability does not imply either capability.\n3552\t\n3553\t#### 8.10.2 Callable representation and identity\n3554\t\n3555\tKeep the callable's existing identity and source-specific data. Add the\n3556\tcommon entry beside its private code and metadata:\n3557\t\n3558\t```clojure\n3559\t;; Illustrative contents of one task-owned Python function cell.\n3560\t;; `entry` and `body-code` are live Yin closures, not literal AST maps.\n3561\t{:yang.call/entry entry\n3562\t :py/type :function\n3563\t :spec parameter-spec\n3564\t :defaults defaults\n3565\t :code body-code}\n3566\t```\n3567\t\n3568\tThe existing `:code` field is not the shared entry: its signature differs\n3569\tbetween preludes. It may remain private. Cross-language callers must not\n3570\tinspect it or extract it to bypass the entry.\n3571\t\n3572\tA cell-backed callable stores the entry in its cell contents. An\n3573\timmutable callable descriptor, such as a bound method, may carry it\n3574\tdirectly in its map. The common prelude projects the entry structurally:\n3575\tread an existing sealed cell reference through `cell/get`, or inspect\n3576\tthe immutable descriptor, then obtain `:yang.call/entry`. It must not\n3577\tdispatch on `:py/type`, `:js/type`, `:php/type`, language names, or a\n3578\tregistry of languages.\n3579\t\n3580\tAn admitted callable is a runtime cell/descriptor constructed or exposed\n3581\tby the callable constructors or import/export projections of a pinned,\n3582\tconforming profile. The entry slot is a runtime descriptor field, not a\n3583\tsource property that promotes arbitrary data to a function. A Python\n3584\tdictionary, JavaScript object, or PHP array containing a source key\n3585\tspelled `:yang.call/entry` remains ordinary source data unless an explicit\n3586\tprofile-defined projection makes it a callable descriptor. Source\n3587\tproperty access must not overwrite or masquerade as this runtime slot.\n3588\tThis is an obligation of construction and source resolution, not a new\n3589\tVM type, descriptor seal, or runtime provenance/language registry. Once\n3590\tthe resolved descriptor is admitted, the shared projection is structural;\n3591\tUAST deliberately constructing a conforming descriptor opts into the\n3592\tconvention rather than changing a source language's data-map semantics.\n3593\t\n3594\tMissing entry means not callable. Constructors must install a genuine\n3595\tunary Yin closure, and supported source mutations must preserve that\n3596\tinvariant. Unary arity is a constructor/profile conformance obligation,\n3597\tnot a signature introspection operation: Yin closures are opaque and the\n3598\tVM's existing argument binding does not enforce this convention's arity.\n3599\tA key in a map grants no VM privilege; application, ownership, and\n3600\teffect checks still apply. A non-applicable entry remains an operational\n3601\tVM application defect, not a source exception caught by the shared helper.\n3602\t\n3603\tFor callable kinds whose eligibility can change, the same cell or\n3604\tdescriptor may also contain `:yang.call/eligible?`, a unary Yin predicate\n3605\ton the original callable. Without it, an entry is eligible by default.\n3606\tWith it, the common callable test uses its boolean result. The predicate\n3607\treads explicit runtime metadata/heap only; it must not mutate state,\n3608\tevaluate arguments, execute the target body, or invoke getters/user hooks.\n3609\tIt has the same constructor/arity obligations as the entry. For example,\n3610\tan instance can keep one dispatch entry while eligibility follows whether\n3611\tits class currently supplies a supported call method; changing the class\n3612\tdoes not require rewriting every instance.\n3613\t\n3614\tCall eligibility is tested at the callability-check point required by\n3615\tthe caller's source, not universally before argument evaluation. The\n3616\tentry resolves/rechecks a dynamic target at its source-required dispatch\n3617\tpoint so argument side effects that change eligibility remain visible.\n3618\tStatic callable kinds need no predicate.\n3619\t\n3620\tSource callable designators, such as PHP function-name strings and\n3621\tcallable arrays where supported, are resolved under their source's rules\n3622\tbefore common invocation. They do not gain entry slots merely by being\n3623\tstrings or arrays. Exporting a designator as a first-class callable needs\n3624\tan explicit frontend projection to an admitted descriptor, retaining any\n3625\tsource-required late lookup and receiver semantics. Passing the raw\n3626\tstring or array as data leaves it unchanged; a foreign caller must not\n3627\tguess its language or search an ambient namespace to invoke it. This is\n3628\tsource resolution/projection, not a language-pair wrapper around an\n3629\talready admitted function.\n3630\t\n3631\tCross-language passage must not allocate a replacement function cell.\n3632\tReturned functions retain their original identity, captures, defaults,\n3633\tbound receiver, properties, and static state. A receiving frontend's\n3634\tcallable test follows this common eligibility rule rather than rejecting\n3635\tforeign native tags. Foreign attribute access and type reflection remain\n3636\tprofile-owned; callability grants no general right to interpret another\n3637\truntime's cell layout.\n3638\t\n3639\tCompiler-internal lambdas and host functions do not acquire this\n3640\tconvention merely by being applicable in Yin. A source import exposing\n3641\tone must emit an entry from its declared signature and effect profile.\n3642\tIt must not guess an opaque closure's signature or bypass host-effect\n3643\tand custody rules. Internal helper calls need not construct records.\n3644\t\n3645\t#### 8.10.3 Invocation record\n3646\t\n3647\tThe invocation is an ephemeral in-machine value. These keys are proposed\n3648\tvocabulary, not existing repository APIs:\n3649\t\n3650\t```clojure\n3651\t{:yang.call/callee     f\n3652\t :yang.call/positional [v0 v1 ...]\n3653\t :yang.call/named      [[\"name\" value] ...]\n3654\t :yang.call/raise      raise-exit\n3655\t ;; Optional: presence means a receiver was supplied, even when nil.\n3656\t :yang.call/receiver   receiver\n3657\t ;; Optional: pinned argument-binding extension, for example locations.\n3658\t :yang.call/binding-profile \"<content-address>\"}\n3659\t```\n3660\t\n3661\tThe four required fields mean:\n3662\t\n3663\t- `:yang.call/callee`: the original resolved callable, including its\n3664\t  identity. The invocation helper supplies it; an extracted entry must\n3665\t  not be applied to another object's substituted state.\n3666\t- `:yang.call/positional`: a dense ordered vector of evaluated values.\n3667\t  Its length records presence; no missing-argument sentinel is inserted.\n3668\t- `:yang.call/named`: ordered name/value pairs, not a map. Names are\n3669\t  plain text without caller-side case folding or normalization.\n3670\t  Duplicate names remain visible until the callee's binder decides them.\n3671\t- `:yang.call/raise`: this activation's caller-supplied, non-returning\n3672\t  guest exit, accepting the condition in section 8.10.7. It closes over\n3673\t  the caller's continuation and exception machinery, never a host"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_CWmx7D3flGgEeNb2O2UCBaBM","content":"1060\t        outcome (symbol (str reserved-prefix \"entry_outcome\"))\n1061\t        positional (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/positional))\n1062\t        named (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/named))\n1063\t        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1064\t        binding-error (outcome-node\n1065\t                        error-tag\n1066\t                        (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1067\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/message)\n1068\t                               (u/lit \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\")\n1069\t                               (u/lit :yin.k/data)\n1070\t                               (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1071\t                                      (u/lit :yang.call/named) named)))\n1072\t        entry-body (u/let1\n1073\t                     outcome\n1074\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1075\t                                (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1076\t                                binding-error)\n1077\t                     (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1078\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 0))\n1079\t                                       (u/lit ok-tag))\n1080\t                                (u/app (u/v 'data/nth) (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))\n1081\t                                (u/app raise\n1082\t                                       (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/thrown)\n1083\t                                              (u/app (u/v 'data/nth)\n1084\t                                                     (u/v outcome) (u/lit 1))))))\n1085\t        ;; The private lane forwards the body's outcome in tail position.\n1086\t        ;; The public entry still converts outcomes to value/raise normally.\n1087\t        entry (u/lam [invocation]\n1088\t                     (u/if-node\n1089\t                       (u/app (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n1090\t                              (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation)\n1091\t                                     (u/lit :clj/outcome-token))\n1092\t                              (u/v 'dsg__call_token))\n1093\t                       (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'dsg__empty) named)\n1094\t                                  (u/app (u/v body) positional)\n1095\t                                  binding-error)\n1096\t                       entry-body))]\n1097\t    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n1098\t\n1099\t\n1100\t(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n1101\t  \"Admit a descriptor constructed by trusted UAST/profile code. This is not\n1102\t   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n1103\t  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n1104\t  (let [descriptor-name 'dsg__descriptor\n1105\t        canonical (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) descriptor-ast\n1106\t                         (u/lit :clj/admission) (u/lit nil))\n1107\t        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private\n1108\t        ;; token. Projection reconstructs and compares that opaque closure;\n1109\t        ;; it never applies a source-supplied predicate. An equal immutable\n1110\t        ;; reconstruction is the same value, not admission of different data.\n1111\t        witness (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_admission) (u/v descriptor-name))\n1112\t        published (u/let1 descriptor-name canonical\n1113\t                          (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v descriptor-name)\n1114\t                                 (u/lit :clj/admission) witness))]\n1115\t    (cond-> (u/mark-tails published)\n1116\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n1117\t\n1118\t\n1119\t(defn- compile-call-descriptor\n1120\t  \"Publish a private body through a canonical constructor-created entry.\"\n1121\t  [body-ast tail?]\n1122\t  (admit-call-descriptor\n1123\t    (u/app (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/lit {})\n1124\t           (u/lit :yang.call/entry) (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_entry) body-ast)\n1125\t           (u/lit :clj/type) (u/lit :function)\n1126\t           (u/lit :clj/outcomes?) (u/lit true))\n1127\t    tail?))\n1128\t\n1129\t\n1130\t(defn- compile-av-fn\n1131\t  \"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\n1132\t   `fn-name` names the function in an arity error outcome. Under the outcome\n1133\t   model the published value is an immutable common-call descriptor.\"\n1134\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env nil nil))\n1135\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env fn-name nil))\n1136\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name source]\n1137\t   (let [arities (mapv (fn [{:keys [params body]}]\n1138\t                         (check-av-params! params)\n1139\t                         {:n (count params)\n1140\t                          :form (av-let env macro-env params body)})\n1141\t                       arities)\n1142\t         body (compile-lambda [av-sym] (av-dispatch env fn-name source arities)\n1143\t                              env false macro-env)]\n1144\t     (if (outcomes? env)\n1145\t       (compile-call-descriptor body tail?)\n1146\t       (cond-> body tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\n1147\t\n1148\t\n1149\t(defn- fn-arities\n1150\t  \"Arities of (fn [params] body*) or (fn ([params] body*)+) operands.\"\n1151\t  [operands]\n1152\t  (cond\n1153\t    (vector? (first operands))\n1154\t    [{:params (first operands), :body (rest operands)}]\n1155\t\n1156\t    (and (seq operands) (every? #(and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) operands))\n1157\t    (mapv (fn [a] {:params (first a), :body (rest a)}) operands)\n1158\t\n1159\t    :else (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params (first operands)})))"}
