{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_E9QRNvCWfPo1dRZAMlE0QrbS","content":"collab/yang-clojure/1793309000000-engineer-adopt-fix1.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:6:Added bounded validation and execution checks around the oracle checkpoint round-trip. Confirmed the regression stops the old sequencing at 100,001 validation visits.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793386000000-reviewer-adopt-fix-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md:18:**P3-2 named-argument classification — CLOSED (conformant per ruling (e); not re-raised, no new evidence).** Probe: `(yang.call/invoke f [] [[\"x\" 1]] raise)` → `[:yang.call/thrown \"Clojure functions do not accept named arguments\" [[\"x\" 1]]]` — reason, message and the named payload round-trip intact, as ruled.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793386000000-reviewer-adopt-fix-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md:26:**P2 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1299 (native-name? branch, via :588) + src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:22,33-40 | Admission bypass at the protocol front door: `yang.call/invoke`/`invoke-with` skip the witness gate.** Namespaced operators are `native-name?`-true, so source calls to `yang.call/invoke` and `yang.call/invoke-with` compile through the direct native application branch and never pass `dsg__admitted?`; the runtime `yang.call/eligible?` they consult is structural **by design** (\"Descriptor projection remains structural after callable admission\", call.cljc:22). Probes: `(let [h (assoc {} :yang.call/entry (get f :yang.call/entry))] (yang.call/invoke h [21] [] raise))` → **`[:yin.k/ok 42]`** — the forged callee runs (same via `invoke-with`); control with the real `f` → 42, so the surface itself is legitimate and corpus-exercised. Sharper shapes: guest-fn or scalar entries forged the same way → raw host **\"Cannot apply non-function\"** — a defect, not a condition — the exact class ruling (c) said must not surface. Mitigations found: admitted-but-ineligible profiles still refuse through the runtime predicate hook, and the copied entry only re-runs its original body (no privilege escalation demonstrated — the forged callable is behaviorally the original). Still, ruling (a) states the boundary absolutely (\"Copying :yang.call/entry into it must not make it callable\"), and the copy IS callable here. Fix (either): extend the clojure.cljc:1286 compile-branch pattern to `invoke`/`invoke-with` so their callee operand is witness-gated (smallest change: one more branch case), or record with the architect that the protocol's own front door is the sanctioned profile-level construction channel, with a ledger row plus fixtures pinning exactly what it admits and that non-closure entries refuse with a qualified condition rather than a host defect.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793386000000-reviewer-adopt-fix-r2.glm-5.3.findings.md:49:| P3-2 named-arg classification | (e) conformant, not re-raised | **CLOSED (conformant)** — payload round-trip intact |\ncollab/orchestration/architect-shared-observation-core-r9.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:588:declaration-driven totality over `outcomes-next`, members round-trip through\ncollab/orchestration/1789418467300-architect-tuples-revision-r8.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:26:round (round-trip law below).\ncollab/orchestration/1789418467300-architect-tuples-revision-r8.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:64:7. **The round-trip law is a first-class conformance obligation:** for every\ncollab/orchestration/1789418467300-architect-tuples-revision-r8.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:82:  round-trip law — and the rows, not the map, are what persists, travels, and\ncollab/orchestration/1789418467300-architect-tuples-revision-r8.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:117:- **§10**: blockers stand; add the round-trip law where §7.2 lands it.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793770000001-engineer-h3-0-codex.findings.md:1:# H3-0 findings\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793770000001-engineer-h3-0-codex.findings.md:7:Focused commands use `clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:h3 {:main-opts [\"/private/tmp/h3-unit.clj\"]}}}' -M:test:h3` and analogous scripts, to avoid test-runner discovery of unrelated Python tests whose generated `Python3Lexer` is absent. Unit result: `{:test 3, :pass 18, :fail 0, :error 0}` for accounting, writer round-trip and unused-arity/poisoned-parse regression. A subsequent current-source accounting/writer run gave `{:test 2, :pass 10, :fail 0, :error 0}`. `clj -M:kondo --lint test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`: `linting took 623ms, errors: 0, warnings: 0` (before final minor test edits; rerun below). `git diff --check` produced no output.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:16:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1918-1926** | `kind-arities` publishes `'var? [1]` unconditionally (line 1926) while `kind-module` provides `var?` only under `#?(:clj … :default {})` (line 1920) — on a Node/Dart host the arity profile would admit a binding the module cannot supply. Relatedly, metadata attached via the new `kind/with-meta` seam has no stated serialization-survival guarantee: no fixture round-trips a meta'd value through the store/encoder, so `meta` after restoration is unspecified. | Fix: gate the published arity with the same reader conditional (or register the capability per-host at harness setup), and add a note/obligation that host metadata is not a serialized ABI field.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793309500000-reviewer-adopt-s1.glm-5.3.findings.md:18:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1035-1042, 1052-1055 | Named-argument binding errors ride `:yang.call/thrown`.** The nonempty-named rejection produces a slice-5 error map raised as a `:yang.call/thrown` condition, indistinguishable at the caller from a guest throw; 8.10.7 (yang.antlr.md:3852-3858) provides qualified reasons (e.g. `:yang.call/unsupported-binding`) for callee binding failures. Data is preserved either way (probes confirmed message/data/named round-trip), so informational.\ncollab/dao-star/1793038927884-reviewer-dao-star-cart-confirm-low.gpt-6-1-sol.findings.md:5:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/clj/dao/star_cart/grid_effects.clj | sed -n '45,115p'; nl -ba test/dao/star_cart/fixes_test.clj | sed -n '95,155p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    45\\t(defn- check-name\\n    46\\t  [n]\\n    47\\t  (when-not (and (string? n) (<= 1 (count (str/trim n)) max-name))\\n    48\\t    (reject! (str \\\"name must be 1-\\\" max-name \\\" characters\\\")))\\n    49\\t  (str/trim n))\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\t\\n    52\\t(defn- check-image\\n    53\\t  \\\"The canonical DECODED image path.  An encoded spelling (`%20`) is decoded\\n    54\\t   once here, so the catalog stores the file's real path and the view encodes it\\n    55\\t   exactly once.\\\"\\n    56\\t  [root url]\\n    57\\t  (when-not (and (string? url) (<= (count url) 300) (str/starts-with? url \\\"/images/\\\"))\\n    58\\t    (reject! \\\"image must be an /images/ path\\\"))\\n    59\\t  (let [decoded (or (edge/decode-path url) (reject! \\\"image path is malformed\\\"))]\\n    60\\t    (when-not (re-matches #\\\"/images/[^/]+\\\" decoded)\\n    61\\t      ;; single segment under /images/, so dot-segment and repeated-separator\\n    62\\t      ;; aliases (`/images/./x`, `/images/a/../b`, `/images//x`) are refused\\n    63\\t      ;; before storage and duplicate comparison (review LOW, 2026-10-27)\\n    64\\t      (reject! \\\"image path aliases are not accepted\\\"))\\n    65\\t    (when-not (edge/static-file root decoded)\\n    66\\t      (reject! \\\"image file does not exist\\\"))\\n    67\\t    decoded))\\n    68\\t\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t(defn- check-tagory\\n    71\\t  [n]\\n    72\\t  (when-not (and (string? n) (<= 1 (count (str/trim n)) max-tagory))\\n    73\\t    (reject! (str \\\"tagory must be 1-\\\" max-tagory \\\" characters\\\")))\\n    74\\t  (str/trim n))\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\t(defn- edit-tx\\n    78\\t  \\\"tx-data for `changes` on item `slug` under `db`, or a rejection.\\\"\\n    79\\t  [root db slug changes]\\n    80\\t  (let [eid (or (catalog/item-eid db slug) (reject! \\\"no such item\\\"))\\n    81\\t        current (catalog/item db slug)\\n    82\\t        ;; an unchanged value is not transacted: re-asserting a card-one\\n    83\\t        ;; value would retract and assert the same datom in one tx\\n    84\\t        changed (fn [k v] (when (not= v (get current k)) v))]\\n    85\\t    (vec\\n    86\\t      (concat\\n    87\\t        (when (some? (:name changes))\\n    88\\t          (when-some [n (changed :name (check-name (:name changes)))]\\n    89\\t            [[:db/add eid :item/name n]]))\\n    90\\t        (when (some? (:price changes))\\n    91\\t          (let [p (parse-price (:price changes))]\\n    92\\t            (when-not (<= 0 p max-price) (reject! \\\"price out of range\\\"))\\n    93\\t            (when-some [p' (changed :price p)]\\n    94\\t              [[:db/add eid :item/price p']])))\\n    95\\t        (when (some? (:description changes))\\n    96\\t          (let [d (:description changes)]\\n    97\\t            (when-not (and (string? d) (<= (count d) max-description))\\n    98\\t              (reject! (str \\\"description must be at most \\\" max-description \\\" characters\\\")))\\n    99\\t            (when-some [d' (changed :description d)]\\n   100\\t              [[:db/add eid :item/description d']])))\\n   101\\t        (when (contains? changes :add-image)\\n   102\\t          (let [u (check-image root (:add-image changes))]\\n   103\\t            (when (catalog/image-eid db slug u) (reject! \\\"image already on the item\\\"))\\n   104\\t            [{:db/id \\\"tid_new_image\\\" :image/url u}\\n   105\\t             [:db/add eid :item/images \\\"tid_new_image\\\"]]))\\n   106\\t        (when (contains? changes :remove-image)\\n   107\\t          (let [i (or (catalog/image-eid db slug (:remove-image changes))\\n   108\\t                      (reject! \\\"image is not on the item\\\"))]\\n   109\\t            [[:db/retract eid :item/images i retract-meta]]))\\n   110\\t        (when (contains? changes :add-tagory)\\n   111\\t          (let [n (check-tagory (:add-tagory changes))]\\n   112\\t            (when (catalog/tagory-linked? db slug n) (reject! \\\"tagory already on the item\\\"))\\n   113\\t            (if-let [t (catalog/tagory-eid db n)]\\n   114\\t              [[:db/add eid :item/tagories t]]\\n   115\\t              [{:db/id \\\"tid_new_tagory\\\" :tagory/name n}\\n    95\\t    (is (= 2 @calls))\\n    96\\t    (let [fresh (store/open {:seed (:test-path st)})]\\n    97\\t      (is (= [11 22] (mapv #(:price (store/item fresh %)) [\\\"a\\\" \\\"b\\\"]))\\n    98\\t          \\\"the file carries both edits, not an older snapshot\\\"))))\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t\\n   101\\t;; 5. image urls\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t(deftest an-encoded-image-spelling-is-stored_decoded_and-served\\n   104\\t  (let [st (fixture [(item \\\"a\\\")])\\n   105\\t        real \\\"/images/P-141  Green Camouflage.png\\\"\\n   106\\t        encoded \\\"/images/P-141%20%20Green%20Camouflage.png\\\"]\\n   107\\t    (is (.isFile (io/file asset-root (subs real 1))) \\\"the premise: this file exists\\\")\\n   108\\t    (is (= {:saved \\\"a\\\"} (fx/apply-edit! st asset-root {:item \\\"a\\\" :changes {:add-image encoded}})))\\n   109\\t    (is (some #{real} (:images (store/item st \\\"a\\\"))) \\\"stored as the canonical decoded path\\\")\\n   110\\t    (is (= encoded (v/enc-path real)) \\\"encoded exactly once for the page\\\")\\n   111\\t    (let [site (edge/make-edge {:asset-root asset-root :shop identity :grid identity})]\\n   112\\t      (is (= 200 (:status (site {:uri encoded :request-method :get})))))\\n   113\\t    (testing \\\"the other spellings of it are the same image\\\"\\n   114\\t      (is (= {:rejected \\\"image already on the item\\\"}\\n   115\\t             (fx/apply-edit! st asset-root {:item \\\"a\\\" :changes {:add-image real}})))\\n   116\\t      (is (= {:rejected \\\"image already on the item\\\"}\\n   117\\t             (fx/appl