 criteria. \"Phase 3 is not a prerequisite\" conflicts with \"both decision gates\" being prerequisites: the descriptor key-set gate is Phase 3's decision gate and is fed by Phase 3's round-trip evidence. | State that Phase 3's decision gate (not its directory test fixture) is a prerequisite of R3. |\ncollab/dao-space/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:286:a stream round-trip `[T→D]`; P3 opening fetches exactly one blob, zero nodes\ncollab/dao-space/1788874487255-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:558:| 8 | `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream` (:759; 783, plus the carrier at 777) | the coordinate is plain EDN, exact-bounded, carries the EAVT comparator, travels through a stream, and opens on the far side — P2 | **Moved and modernized.** Keep the `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip and the carrier — now a **v2** ring buffer — and open the transported coordinate with `query/open-published!`. `ds/exact-bound?` (:779) is v1; replace it with a direct assertion on `{:manifest-address …}`, which is what P1 fixes anyway. |\ncollab/dao-star/1793037435251-stream-engineer-dao-star-cart-fixes.prompt.md:46:Test: an encoded spelling of an existing filename round-trips to a working\ncollab/dao-space/1789289033041-runtime-review-index-as-observer-r2.glm-5.3.prompt.md:16:- **F1** — Phase 0′ now round-trips the *checkpoint value* `{:manifest-address :cursor :ids :batch}` and compares `restored-indexes` over the published manifest to the live trees as sets; the live-session round trip is gone, with your reason stated.\ncollab/core-datom/1789670000000-architect-code-as-tuples-implementation-plan.prompt.md:56:   claims item 13 (the round-trip law) is \"testable now\" because the map-\ncollab/core-datom/1789670000000-architect-code-as-tuples-implementation-plan.prompt.md:60:   buildable unit and the round-trip test is its own acceptance criterion,\ncollab/dao-jing/1789924845000-storage-engineer-deb