h with zero attaches. The old codec and inspector are untouched.\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/7b-review.md:26:8. **Portability read.** No `for`, no private-var access across namespaces, catches `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)` everywhere new, `#?(:cljd … :clj …)` order kept, `(assoc {} …)` starts, no unary float minus, no EDN strings. Base64 through `jing/bytes->base64`/`base64->bytes` (the shared `dao.stream` codec, all hosts); byte equality by `(vec …)`; `integer?` on CBOR-decoded counters is host-safe for whole numbers. `yin.vm.engine/…` is never referenced from `export.cljc` (the surviving M02c mutant used it; the production file does not). `(:yin.link/id response)` and `parent` round-trip CBOR as vectors of keyword and int on every host. Unverified on Node/Dart by instruction.\ncollab/core-datom/1789272850107-review-macro-system-v2.kimi-k3.findings.md:93:- **Macro representation round-trips today** (`:yin/macro?`, `:yin/phase-policy` with `:compile` default; embedded-lambda operators deduped to one entity) exactly as §2.1 states.\ncollab/dao-stream/1790655248000-vm-engineer-ffi-caller-correlation.claude-opus-5-5.report.md:114:2. **Token domain: a non-blank string or a keyword.** glm listed uuid, but a uuid fails `vm/plain-data?`, which the prompt also requires. I chose plain data. `vm.cljc` validates the format at construction. `caller/open` also checks a round-trip of `[token :parked-0]` through an optional `::codec`. **Uniqueness per tenure is the composition's duty.** Nothing can verify it locally.\ncollab/dao-stream/1790655248000-vm-engineer-ffi-caller-correlation.claude-opus-5-5.report.md:149:- CLJD was excluded by instruction. The vector-key round-trip test is in place for when that lane runs.\ncollab/general/scratch-2026-10/1791497000000-architect-subsystem-test-spec.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:38:- low | test/yang/python/antlr/int_contract_fixtures.cljc | required by `dao.jing.stream-test`, `dao.stream.journal-test`, `yin.vm.ucf.scalar-round-trip-test`; three layer-0/2 tests name a layer-3 namespace; the fixture reaches no ANTLR class so no build cost | move to a neutral `test/` home; open question 2.\ncollab/dao-stream/1792485300000-engineer-codec-c0.claude-sonnet-5-5.findings.md:13:- `test/dao/stream/codec_test.cljc`: gate (modern/legacy/dual accepted, malformed rejected), accessors, D accept/reject corpus (§4.4 adversarial identifier, direct/nested symbol-metadata, record cases), law over `cbor/profile` and `transit/profile`, CBOR-only list round-trip.\ncollab/dao-stream/1792485300000-engineer-codec-c0.claude-sonnet-5-5.findings.md:35:The §4.4 law does not hold for **lists on Transit on the JVM**: `'(1 2)` is in D and Transit's `portable-value?` accepts it, but Transit's `decode` returns a non-list seq, which its own `ensure-portable!` (`list?`) rejects (`ExceptionInfo {:value (1 2)}` at `transit.cljc:69`). The design text says `'(1 2)` round-trips on both. I removed lists from the shared law corpus and pinned them CBOR-only (`lists-in-d-round-trip-on-cbor`, commented) instead of changing Transit, which this slice leaves unchanged. Needs a decision: narrow D, fix Transit decode, or accept the asymmetry in §4.4. Not checked on cljs/cljd.\ncollab/general/1789556877627-review-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:4:# Review: ClojureDart round-trip-law content-addressing fix\ncollab/orchestration/1789558361866-architect-signoff-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:6:# Architect sign-off: ClojureDart content-addressing round-trip-law fix\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:582:`records`); `log_test.cljc`'s `log-round-trip`, `log-positional-read`,\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:760:- **members round-trip**: `(observer-state (remove-nth (:members st) i))`\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:781:- put then get round-trips through `step`; duplicate put completes `:present`;\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:783:  `{:found? true :value \"hello\"}` round-trip exactly.\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:820:`client-state`. Prove: put and get round-trip over the wire; two clients see\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-v2-revision-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:1037:- `dao.jing.v2.remote` round-trips put, get and **materialize** through\ncollab/core-datom/architect-staged-docs-r1.all-findings.md:163:None of the ten invariants (contract:64–79) mentions identity, descriptors, or portability. Yet below them the contract asserts: identity \"is universal and outlives any attachment, so `descriptor` has no failure outcome\" (194–196); \"the same descriptor attaches to the same stream every time\" (240–241); \"`ok` — identity outlives any attachment\" (474). Ask which of the ten yields these — none does. Likewise the Surfaces clause \"A deposit destination must admit every valid boundary event… wiring one that can refuse is a host assembly defect\" (344–348) is imported from the authority's Host Boundaries section, not derived from the ten. These aren't corners: Phase 3's entire round-trip deliverable and ws's ended-stream semantics rest on the identity guarantees. As a governance rule (\"a proposed addition that cannot be derived… does not belong\"), the claim would reject a legitimate future identity clause or accept these by silent exception.\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791254000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d11-writer.findings.md:79:  *mechanical*, no architect round-trip needed: the ungated sweep's\ncollab/dao-space/1789289033041-runtime-review-index-as-observer.glm-5.3.findings.md:6:- **2 P2 findings**: (F1) Phase 0′'s `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip test premise is false — a live session isn't plain data (`BTSet` prints elements-only and reads back as a host set; `:storage` prints unreadably); (F2) draining the recording handle is unsafe on the resumed-checkpoint path on the JVM — `-store-tree!` overwrites the wrapper's restore source (`btree.cljc:1253`) with the recording handle, and a soft-ref'd root then refaults through the drained handle → \"missing index segment\".\ncollab/dao-space/1789289033041-runtime-review-index-as-observer.glm-5.3.findings.md:38:- 2 P2 findings (pr-str round-trip test premise false; JVM root-refault\ncollab/dao-space/1789289033041-runtime-review-index-as-observer.glm-5.3.findings.md:108:The mechanisms are portable: `dao.space.index` is one `.cljc` requiring only `.cljc` deps (`index.cljc:35-39`); the additions are atoms, integers, keywords, btree values, and pure functions; `compare-vals` is already host-conditionaled (`index.cljc:57-74`); `kv-storage`'s default ref-type is per-host with `:strong` off-JVM (`btree.cljc:39-44`), so cljs/cljd never even see the soft-ref behavior behind F2; `dao.stream.observer` is one `.cljc`. What does **not** hold cross-platform (or anywhere): Phase 0′'s `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip premise (F1).\ncollab/dao-space/1789289033041-runtime-review-index-as-observer.glm-5.3.findings.md:114:**[P2 — must address] F1. Phase 0′'s serialization test premise is false: a live session is not plain data.** `dao.space.index.as-observer.md:414-416` tests \"ids stable across a `pr-str`/`read-string` round trip of the session (it is plain data plus btree values)\". A `BTSet` prints as `#{…}` — elements only (`btree.cljc:1500-1512`) — and reads back as a *host* set: comparator, `:storage`, address marks and `cnt` are all gone (so `subseq-from` on the result fails); the session's `:storage` is a `KVStorage` over closures (`storage.cljc:38-62`) that prints as an unreadable `#object` on `:clj` (read-string throws), and the `:observer`'s stream handle is no more printable. No reader/tag exists for any of this. The test item needs redefining — round-trip the *checkpoint* value, or assert equality of `restored-indexes` against a re-opened manifest — before Phase 0′ can start.\ncollab/dao-space/1789289033041-runtime-review-index-as-observer.glm-5.3.findings.md:139:- **2 P2 findings**: (F1) Phase 0′'s `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip test premise is false — a live session isn't plain data (`BTSet` prints elements-only and reads back as a host set; `:storage` prints unreadably); (F2) draining the recording handle is unsafe on the resumed-checkpoint path on the JVM — `-store-tree!` overwrites the wrapper's restore source (`btree.cljc:1253`) with the recording handle, and a soft-ref'd root then refaults through the drained handle → \"missing index segment\".\ncollab/dao-jing/1789572268000-review-jing-cbor-design-r3.glm-5.3.findings.md:18:**B — Sound and forced by A; not too restrictive.** Under portable equality, `{1 :a, 1.0 :b}` cannot round-trip: the canonical bytes keep both entries (integer vs `dao.jing/float64` are distinct encodings), but the decoded map on any host applying portable `=` collapses them — `decode(encode(m)) ≠ m`, which the acceptance criteria forbid. The only alternatives are host-sensitive acceptance (JVM keeps both entries, Node collapses — exactly the divergence the revision refuses) or abandoning mathematical equality. The pre-decode rejection (\"before decoded collection construction\") is the load-bearing half: without it, the accepting host's map constructor would silently decide the boundary. The only values lost are ones that could never satisfy the round-trip acceptance — the same standing rule as \"reject duplicates introduced by normalization.\"\ncollab/dao-space/1788961984449-review-space-index-phase3.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:25:| #8 | Portable coordinate and carrier round-trip | `query_test.cljc:1032` checks EDN equality, the complete coordinate map, successful v2 carrier append/read, and reopening with the expected rows. |\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791236000000-reviewer-d9-v1-lift-gate.prompt.md:47:   record round-trips the canonical codec and re-encodes identically;\ncollab/dao-stream/1790532500000-vm-engineer-node-ws-test-migration.glm-flash.report.md:7:- **a-reflection-round-trips...** (`a-reflection-verified` :496-514): asserts the real 5-event sequence `[:ws/opened]` + 4 `[:ws/payload]` envelopes — descriptor-probe answer with asker-minted id 0 carrying `:dao.stream.remote/surface #{:writer :reader}`, the append!'s source ok, the cursor mint (`:dao.stream/cursor` present), and the next carrying `\"hello\"`; replaces the stale 2-event assertion (:486 old). Correlation fixed (:443 `channel-attachment`): the old `(:dao.stream/attachment (:attach client))` was the *remote* attacher's uuid; envelopes carry the ws attachment from `(project/channel dial)`.\ncollab/yin-ucf/1790851062697-vm-engineer-d7-host-typed-closures.claude-opus-5-5.report-r2.md:78:- `semantic_test` now round-trips the continuation's payload through EDN, not the continuation itself.\ncollab/dao-jing/reviewer-jing-invariant-completeness.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:42:| `opaque-payloads-round-trip-including-nil` | B4, B5 | mapped |\ncollab/dao-jing/reviewer-jing-invariant-completeness.gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md:51:| `codec-test` | F1, B5, F7 | partially mapped — tuple/nil round-trip is covered semantically, but direct `encode-record`/`decode-record` and exact framing are intentionally dropped |\ncollab/core-datom/1790796340212-reviewer-data-primitives-gate.glm-5.3.findings.md:65:surrogates, U+10FFFF round-trip, empty strings all pinned); cross-host\ncollab/dao-stream/1790566005000-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r10.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md:29:   migration/round-trip/retained-entry tests; the lift pin asserts\ncollab/dao-stream/1790566005000-architect-dao-stream-remote-slice8-confirm-r10.gpt-6-sol.prompt.md:31:   round-trip pin asserts the lowered :datom = original envelope; a\ncollab/dao-space/1788949213827-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:438:a stream round-trip `[T→D]`; P3 opening fetches exactly one blob, zero nodes\ncollab/dao-space/1788949213827-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r4.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:707:| 8 | `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream` (:759; 783, carrier :777) | P2 | **Moved and modernized.** Keep the `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip and the carrier, now a v2 ring buffer (§4.5), and open the transported coordinate with `query/open-published!`. Assert the **complete exact coordinate map**, not only `:manifest-address`; `ds/exact-bound?` (:779) is v1 and is replaced by that equality. |\ncollab/dao-jing/1790028600000-ref-j2-review-glm.findings.md:18:`test/dao/jing/cbor_test.cljc:77-83`. On Dart a failing `is` throws (cljd.test `is` → package:test `expect`, which throws `TestFailure`), so when a case body's `is` fails inside `guarded`, the catch handler's own `(is false …)` throws in turn and escapes — the `doseq` aborts and every later case in that deftest is hidden. The prompt's test criterion 5 asks whether this is \"handled everywhere, including decode runners\": it is not. Only the two `is false` paths of the encode-refusal runner (`:not-constructible`, `:host-merged`) were converted to collect-and-assert-once (`cbor_test.cljc:114-149`, correct). Still aborting at first failure on Dart: `canonical-cases-encode-and-round-trip` (`:95-111`), `decode-refusal-cases…` (`:152-159`), `groups-hold-on-produced-bytes` (`:162-179`), `encoding-ignores-ambient-print-settings` (`:266-279`), and the refusal-class `is` branches inside encode-refusal (`:133-134`, `:146-147`). Impact is diagnostic only — a mutation still turns the lane red at the first bad case; there is no false-green path. Smallest fix: mirror the encode-refusal pattern — have `guarded` `swap!`-conjure `[id e]` into a shared atom and assert it empty at the end of each runner deftest (or in one trailing deftest), instead of calling `is` inside the catch.\ncollab/dao-space/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:407:a stream round-trip `[T→D]`; P3 opening fetches exactly one blob, zero nodes\ncollab/dao-space/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:659:| 8 | `published-index-is-a-transportable-bounded-stream` (:759; 783, carrier :777) | P2 | **Moved and modernized.** Keep the `pr-str`/`read-string` round-trip and the carrier, now a **v2 ring buffer** (§4.5), and open the transported coordinate with `query/open-published!`. Per the review, assert the **complete exact coordinate map**, not only `:manifest-address`. `ds/exact-bound?` (:779) is v1 and is replaced by that equality. |\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791223000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d9-v1-lift.prompt.md:59:   reader must accept every regenerated v1 fixture (round-trip).\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-cutover-r6.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:373:opens and `count-records`; `log_test.cljc`'s `log-round-trip`,\ncollab/dao-jing/architect-dao-jing-cutover-r6.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:460:  **members round-trip**: `(observer-state (remove-nth (:members st) i))`\ncollab/general/1789558361866-architect-signoff-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.prompt.md:6:# Task: Architect sign-off on the ClojureDart content-addressing round-trip-law fix\ncollab/general/1789558361866-architect-signoff-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.prompt.md:23:- `collab/1789556877627-review-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`\ncollab/general/1789558361866-architect-signoff-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.prompt.md:24:  and `collab/1789556877627-review-round-trip-law-cljd-fix-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`\ncollab/general/1789558361866-architect-signoff-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.prompt.md:32:Root cause: `test/yin/vm_test.cljc`'s `semantic-bytecode-round-trip-law`\ncollab/general/1789558361866-architect-signoff-round-trip-law-cljd-fix.prompt.md:52:Transit follow-up) → the round-trip-law failure is gone after the first\ncollab/dao-jing/1790148097751-storage-engineer-hash-registry-h0.prompt.md:137:   - Keyword addresses round-trip cleanly through Clojure reader/printer across JVM and JS.\ncollab/yin-repl/