{"role":"assistant","content":"## Verdict: REJECT\n\nThe round is not landable or close to landable. Beyond the confirmed malformed `ns` form and nonexistent requires (`REVIEW-h3-0-vibe.diff:22-33`), its central callable guard both rejects the real runtime representation and accepts forged values. It also adds none of the required regression or writer round-trip tests. Keep the pre-existing declarations file, but redo the implementation from the pristine harness.\n\n### 1. Declarations-driven classifier and guards\n\nThe overall direction is reasonable: classification looks up an external, versioned declaration, returns its boundary/reason/provenance fields, and leaves raw outcomes and agreement calculations untouched (`REVIEW-h3-0-vibe.diff:35-69`, `:133-134`). It also validates each C lane independently rather than forcing callable representations to compare equal.\n\nFor the two portability declarations:\n\n- **Pinned fixture ID:** present through `(get-in @declarations [:portability id])`; an undeclared ID cannot classify (`:44-45`).\n- **Exact call:** present (`:46`).\n- **Completed A/B/C:** present for all four lanes (`:48`).\n- **Original message:** checked against the declaration and each C outcome (`:47`, `:52-53`).\n- **A/B agreement:** preserved (`:49`).\n- **Payload and collection shape:** present. Both compare all error data except `:meta`, including `:script`, and use `result-shape` to distinguish vectors from sequences (`:54-57`). The declaration’s separate `:script` field is never read, but the exact call plus payload/shape checks cover the actual script.\n- **Precise host-function boundary:** **missing.** The pristine requirement that A’s `:meta` equal `{:nonportable-host-value (str (class clojure.core/meta))}` was not carried into the new classifier. Consequently, any matching A/B host value can be reclassified as this specific `clojure.core/meta` departure.\n- **Guest-callable validation:** present syntactically but unsound (`:58-63`), as detailed below.\n- **Negative controls:** **not added for this classifier.** The pristine tests still exercise `kernel-host-value-deviation`, while production now calls `declared-portability-boundary?` (`:131-134`). Thus the existing bad-ID, incomplete-lane, changed-payload/shape, and forged-callable tests do not test the new production path. There is no new mutated-call control either.\n\nThe upstream-failure replacement largely preserves the old detailed guards: declaration/ID and exact call (`:74-79`), completed and equal C lanes (`:77-78`), and the specific A/B exception and C refusal checks (`:81-108`). It also returns declared scope, reason, and upstream revision. However, the pristine negative controls still invoke `kernel-upstream-failure`, not `declared-upstream-failure?`, so the replacement is likewise untested.\n\nThere is **no writer or test hunk at all**. Therefore the required write+read coverage for declarations, statuses, raw comparisons, and coverage is absent. The mutable memoizing atom and working-directory-relative `slurp` (`:35-39`) are also unnecessary deviations from the harness’s resource-loading style.\n\n### 2. Accepted callable representations\n\nThe accepted alternatives at `:59-63` and duplicated in the legacy classifier at `:118-123` are:\n\n1. A bare value satisfying `values/closure?`.\n2. Any map with `:type :closure` and merely present `:source` and `:env` keys.\n\nThe second representation is invented for this boundary. The actual refreshed outcomes contain descriptors such as:\n\n```clojure\n{:yang.call/entry <closure>\n :clj/type :function\n :clj/outcomes? true\n :clj/admission <closure>}\n```\n\nSee `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn:82,87` and the constructor at `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1119-1127`. There are no top-level `:source` or `:env` fields. Since a descriptor map is not itself a Yin `Closure`, `values/closure?` is false for it (`src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc:151-155`). Therefore the new guard rejects both genuine after-QED rows.\n\nConversely, this forged value passes the map branch:\n\n```clojure\n{:type :closure :source nil :env nil}\n```\n\n`contains?` checks presence, not value or provenance. This directly violates the forged-callable negative-control requirement.\n\nA sound redo must validate the **actual admitted descriptor**, including genuine closure values in `:yang.call/entry` and `:clj/admission` and the constructor’s admission invariant, not just recognizable keys. The admission logic is at `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1100-1116,2093-2107`; existing source-forgery controls are at `test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1319-1350`. A bare closure may remain a separately justified legacy test representation, but it is not the refreshed §8.10 descriptor and must not substitute for descriptor validation.\n\n### 3. Known-gaps narrative\n\nThe edit is inaccurate and malformed:\n\n- It repeats the prohibited stale baseline **“145/165 credited, 102 agreements”** in the same row as the new target (`REVIEW-h3-0-vibe.diff:9`, repeated at `:17`, `:146`, `:154`).\n- It claims the writer now round-trips declarations, the deviations assertion passes, and **“H3-0 is now closed”** despite no writer tests, no applicable harness, and a classifier that rejects the real descriptor.\n- The same row is appended multiple times; the entire known-gaps patch itself appears twice (`:1-17` and `:138-154`).\n- `slice9_gate.md`, which the brief explicitly requires refreshing, is untouched.\n- Only the provenance, post-slice target counts, and statement that the gate remains blocked match the brief; those are assertions, not verified outcomes.\n\n### Required redo\n\nDiscard all harness and narrative hunks in this diff. Retain `slice9_declarations.edn` as the declaration input and start again from the pristine classifiers. The harness owner/orchestrator should assign a fresh implementation, with the compiler-engineer reviewer specifically approving the descriptor/admission predicate.\n\nThe redo must:\n\n- preserve the original host `clojure.core/meta` marker guard;\n- validate the real admitted descriptor and reject forged/copied/malformed descriptors;\n- retarget all existing negative controls to the new production classifiers and add mutated-call coverage;\n- add temporary-file writer write+read tests without ordinary-test writes;\n- refresh both gate narrative locations with only the 107/58, 100/2/2/2 accounting;\n- run the focused gate, full oracle namespace, and kondo before making any closure claim."}
